parts:
- text: "My previous attempt at a graph-based method using `sc.pp.neighbors` without explicit batch correction performed poorly, as expected after the debugger report clarified the function's usage. The debugger suggested using `bbknn` for batch-aware neighbor computation.\n\nTherefore, I will now submit a solution that explicitly uses `sc.external.pp.bbknn()` which integrates batches using a batch-balanced k-NN graph. This should address the low iLISI score and potentially improve biological preservation metrics.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Scanpy BBKNN UMAP Integration Baseline\"\ntags: \"baseline, bbknn, graph-based, umap, scanpy, external\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission implements a batch integration approach leveraging `scanpy.external.pp.bbknn`. Following standard preprocessing (normalization and log1p transformation) and selection of highly variable genes, PCA is performed. `sc.external.pp.bbknn` is then used to compute a batch-balanced k-nearest neighbor graph,\
    \ and a UMAP embedding is subsequently generated from this corrected graph. This method aims to improve local batch mixing (iLISI) and preserve biological signals more effectively than non-batch-aware graph methods.\ncontent: |\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import numpy as np\n  import bbknn # Explicitly import bbknn for sc.external.pp.bbknn\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Integrate batches in single-cell RNA-seq data using sc.external.pp.bbknn\n      for batch-balanced neighbor finding, followed by UMAP embedding.\n\n      Args:\n          adata: AnnData object with raw UMI counts and batch labels.\n\n      Returns:\n          AnnData with adata.obsm['X_emb'] containing a UMAP embedding\n          from the batch-corrected graph.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"Scanpy BBKNN UMAP Integration: Starting with raw counts, doing own normalization...\")\n\n      # Preprocessing: normalize_total + log1p\n      print(\"\
    \  Normalizing total counts...\")\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n      print(\"  Log1p transform...\")\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n      # Use highly variable genes if available\n      n_hvg = 2000 # The dataset specifies 2000 HVGs\n      if 'batch_hvg' in adata.var.columns:\n          print(f\"  Using batch-aware HVGs ({sum(adata.var['batch_hvg'])} genes)...\")\n          adata = adata[:, adata.var['batch_hvg']].copy()\n      elif n_hvg and adata.n_vars > n_hvg:\n          print(f\"  Selecting {n_hvg} highly variable genes (standard method)...\")\n          sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=n_hvg)\n          adata = adata[:, adata.var.highly_variable].copy()\n      else:\n          print(\"  Using all available genes as HVGs.\")\n          \n      # Compute PCA\n      n_pcs = min(50, adata.n_vars - 1, adata.n_obs - 1)\n      print(f\"  Computing PCA with {n_pcs} components...\")\n      sc.pp.pca(adata, n_comps=n_pcs)\n\n      # Apply BBKNN for batch-balanced\
    \ neighbor graph computation\n      # This performs batch integration by correcting the neighborhood graph\n      print(f\"  Applying sc.external.pp.bbknn with batch_key='batch'...\")\n      sc.external.pp.bbknn(adata, batch_key='batch', n_pcs=n_pcs)\n\n      # Compute UMAP embedding from the BBKNN-corrected graph\n      print(\"  Computing UMAP embedding from BBKNN graph...\")\n      sc.tl.umap(adata)\n\n      # Create output AnnData with the UMAP embedding\n      output = ad.AnnData(\n          obs=adata.obs[[]],\n          var=adata.var[[]],\n          uns={\n              'dataset_id': adata.uns.get('dataset_id', 'unknown'),\n              'normalization_id': adata.uns.get('normalization_id', 'unknown'),\n              'method_id': 'scanpy_bbknn_umap',\n              'bbknn_params': {\n                  'n_pcs': n_pcs,\n                  'batch_key': 'batch',\n                  'embedding_type': 'umap'\n              }\n          },\n          obsm={\n              'X_emb': adata.obsm['X_umap']\n\
    \          }\n      )\n\n      print(f\"✓ Scanpy BBKNN UMAP Integration complete. UMAP embedding shape: {output.obsm['X_emb'].shape}\")\n      return output\n```"
