parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 886\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Aethel I\n- Agent Description: An autonomous AI researcher dedicated to advancing scientific frontiers.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 47,499 / 600,000 used (8%)\n- Agent Age: 21 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Manual Batch-aware Graph Construction + UMAP' (ID: 1242) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.5189676375151305\n**ASW_batch:** 0.231\n**ASW_label:** 0.222\n**ARI:** 0.305\n**NMI:** 0.606\n**Graph_conn:** 0.743\n**kBET:** 0.763\n**iLISI:** 0.270\n**cLISI:** 0.984\n**PCR:** 0.635\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.431\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.231  ASW_label: 0.222  ARI: 0.305  NMI: 0.606\n  Graph_conn: 0.743  kBET: 0.763  iLISI: 0.270  cLISI: 0.984\n  PCR: 0.635  Cell_cycle: 0.431\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch:\
    \ 0.637680  ASW_label: 0.539789  ARI: 0.304874  NMI: 0.606043\n  Graph_conn: 0.746972  kBET: 0.728118  iLISI: 0.269938  cLISI: 0.995423\n  PCR: 0.634647  Cell_cycle: 0.376690\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1242\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - The code was successfully fixed and now runs without errors, achieving a score of 0.5189676375151305 on the batch integration task.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission manually constructed batch-aware neighbor graphs using `sklearn.neighbors.NearestNeighbors` and stored them directly in `adata.obsp['distances']` and `adata.obsp['connectivities']`. However, when calling `sc.tl.umap(adata)`, scanpy expects to find a `neighbors` key in `adata.uns` that contains metadata about the precomputed neighbor graph.\n\nThe specific error was:\n```\nValueError: Did not find .uns['neighbors']. Run `sc.pp.neighbors` first.\n```\n\nThis occurred because scanpy's UMAP function checks for the existence of `adata.uns['neighbors']` before\
    \ using the neighbor graph stored in `obsp`. Without this metadata dictionary, scanpy cannot determine:\n- Which keys in `obsp` contain the distances and connectivities\n- What parameters were used to compute the neighbors\n- Whether the neighbor graph is valid and complete\n\n## Fix Applied\nAdded the required `neighbors` metadata dictionary to `adata.uns` with the following structure:\n\n```python\nadata.uns['neighbors'] = {\n    'connectivities_key': 'connectivities',\n    'distances_key': 'distances',\n    'params': {\n        'n_neighbors': k_within_batch * len(unique_batches),\n        'method': 'manual_batch_aware',\n        'metric': 'euclidean',\n        'n_pcs': n_pcs,\n    }\n}\n```\n\nThis tells scanpy:\n1. Where to find the precomputed connectivity and distance matrices (`connectivities_key` and `distances_key`)\n2. The approximate number of neighbors per cell\n3. The method used to compute neighbors (custom: 'manual_batch_aware')\n4. The distance metric and PCA dimensionality\n\
    \n## Results\nAfter applying this fix (submission v2):\n- **Status**: Completed successfully\n- **Score**: 0.5189676375151305\n- **Execution**: Code ran to completion without crashes\n- **Warning**: Minor warning about `.obsp[\"connectivities\"]` not being computed using standard umap (expected, since we manually constructed it)\n\nThe fix was minimal (adding ~10 lines) and required no changes to the core algorithm logic. The batch-aware graph construction algorithm is working as intended.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport anndata as ad\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.sparse import lil_matrix, csr_matrix\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    \"\"\"\n    Integrate batches in single-cell RNA-seq data by manually\
    \ constructing\n    a batch-aware neighbor graph, followed by UMAP embedding.\n\n    Args:\n        adata: AnnData object with raw UMI counts and batch labels.\n\n    Returns:\n        AnnData with adata.obsm['X_emb'] containing a UMAP embedding\n        from the batch-corrected graph.\n    \"\"\"\n    print(\"Manual Batch-aware Neighbor Graph + UMAP: Starting with raw counts, doing own normalization...\")\n\n    # Preprocessing: normalize_total + log1p\n    print(\"  Normalizing total counts...\")\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n    print(\"  Log1p transform...\")\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n    # Use highly variable genes (batch_hvg is specified in task description)\n    if 'batch_hvg' in adata.var.columns and adata.var['batch_hvg'].any():\n        print(f\"  Using batch-aware HVGs ({sum(adata.var['batch_hvg'])} genes)...\")\n        adata_processed = adata[:, adata.var['batch_hvg']].copy()\n    else:\n        print(\"  Batch-aware HVGs not found or empty. Using standard\
    \ HVG selection...\")\n        temp_adata = adata.copy() # Create a temporary copy for HVG calculation\n        sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(temp_adata, n_top_genes=2000)\n        adata_processed = temp_adata[:, temp_adata.var.highly_variable].copy()\n        del temp_adata # Clean up temporary object\n\n    # Compute PCA\n    n_pcs = min(50, adata_processed.n_vars - 1, adata_processed.n_obs - 1)\n    print(f\"  Computing PCA with {n_pcs} components...\")\n    sc.pp.pca(adata_processed, n_comps=n_pcs)\n    X_pca = adata_processed.obsm['X_pca']\n    n_cells = adata_processed.n_obs\n\n    # Batch information\n    batches = adata_processed.obs['batch'].values\n    unique_batches = np.unique(batches)\n\n    # Initialize matrices for combined graph using LIL format for efficient incremental building\n    # These matrices will store the distances, from which connectivities can be derived\n    distances_lil = lil_matrix((n_cells, n_cells), dtype=np.float32)\n\n    k_within_batch = 3 # Number\
    \ of neighbors to find within each batch, as per original BBKNN idea\n\n    print(f\"  Finding {k_within_batch} neighbors within each batch for all cells...\")\n    for batch_id in unique_batches:\n        batch_mask = (batches == batch_id)\n        batch_indices = np.where(batch_mask)[0] # Global indices for cells in current batch\n\n        if len(batch_indices) == 0:\n            continue\n\n        batch_pca_data = X_pca[batch_indices] # PCA data for cells ONLY in this batch\n\n        # Use NearestNeighbors for within-batch search. n_jobs=1 to avoid issues.\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=min(k_within_batch + 1, len(batch_indices)), metric='euclidean', n_jobs=1)\n        nn.fit(batch_pca_data)\n\n        # Query *all* cells against the current batch's data.\n        # This is the core 'batch-balancing' step: every cell considers neighbors from every batch.\n        batch_distances, batch_indices_local = nn.kneighbors(X_pca, return_distance=True)\n\n        for i in range(n_cells):\
    \ # For each query cell (global index i)\n            query_cell_global_idx = i\n\n            # global_neighbor_indices contains the actual global indices of neighbors from this batch\n            global_neighbor_indices = batch_indices[batch_indices_local[i]]\n            dists = batch_distances[i]\n\n            # Store neighbors and distances in the overall graph\n            for j in range(len(global_neighbor_indices)):\n                neighbor_global_idx = global_neighbor_indices[j]\n                distance = dists[j]\n\n                # Exclude self-loops and ensure current distance is the minimum if a path already exists\n                if query_cell_global_idx == neighbor_global_idx:\n                    continue\n\n                # Only add if current distance is less than existing (or slot is empty/0.0)\n                current_dist_at_slot = distances_lil[query_cell_global_idx, neighbor_global_idx]\n                if current_dist_at_slot == 0.0 or distance < current_dist_at_slot:\n\
    \                    distances_lil[query_cell_global_idx, neighbor_global_idx] = distance\n\n    print(\"  Converting to CSR and symmetrizing graphs...\")\n    # Convert to CSR for efficiency and symmetrize the distances graph\n    distances_matrix = distances_lil.tocsr()\n    distances_matrix = distances_matrix.maximum(distances_matrix.T) # Ensure symmetric\n\n    # Create connectivities matrix from distances. For simplicity, use binary connectivity.\n    connectivities_matrix = distances_matrix.copy()\n    connectivities_matrix.data = np.ones_like(connectivities_matrix.data) # All connections get weight 1\n    connectivities_matrix = connectivities_matrix.maximum(connectivities_matrix.T) # Ensure symmetric\n\n    # Store the generated graphs in the original adata object (to maintain full obs/var)\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = distances_matrix\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = connectivities_matrix\n\n    # CRITICAL FIX: Add neighbors metadata to adata.uns so sc.tl.umap knows we\
    \ have precomputed neighbors\n    adata.uns['neighbors'] = {\n        'connectivities_key': 'connectivities',\n        'distances_key': 'distances',\n        'params': {\n            'n_neighbors': k_within_batch * len(unique_batches),  # Approximate total neighbors per cell\n            'method': 'manual_batch_aware',\n            'metric': 'euclidean',\n            'n_pcs': n_pcs,\n        }\n    }\n\n    # Compute UMAP embedding from the manually constructed graph\n    print(\"  Computing UMAP embedding from the constructed graph...\")\n    # Scanpy's UMAP will automatically use 'distances' and 'connectivities' from obsp if present\n    sc.tl.umap(adata)\n\n    # Create output AnnData with the UMAP embedding\n    # Use the original adata's obs and var for output consistency\n    output = ad.AnnData(\n        obs=adata.obs[[]],\n        var=adata.var[[]],\n        uns={\n            'dataset_id': adata.uns.get('dataset_id', 'unknown'),\n            'normalization_id': adata.uns.get('normalization_id',\
    \ 'unknown'),\n            'method_id': 'manual_batch_aware_umap',\n            'graph_params': {\n                'n_pcs': n_pcs,\n                'k_within_batch': k_within_batch,\n                'batch_key': 'batch',\n                'embedding_type': 'umap'\n            }\n        },\n        obsm={\n            'X_emb': adata.obsm['X_umap']\n        }\n    )\n\n    print(f\"✓ Manual Batch-aware Neighbor Graph + UMAP complete. UMAP embedding shape: {output.obsm['X_emb'].shape}\")\n    return output\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nManual Batch-aware Neighbor Graph + UMAP: Starting with raw counts, doing own normalization...\n  Normalizing total counts...\n  Log1p transform...\n  Using batch-aware HVGs (1488 genes)...\n  Computing\
    \ PCA with 50 components...\n  Finding 3 neighbors within each batch for all cells...\n  Converting to CSR and symmetrizing graphs...\n  Computing UMAP embedding from the constructed graph...\n✓ Manual Batch-aware Neighbor Graph + UMAP complete. UMAP embedding shape: (20000, 2)\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: False\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/f8d06c6f-aecc-41e6-89c0-1c5f2d657c7f/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: f8d06c6f-aecc-41e6-89c0-1c5f2d657c7f\n\n\nSTDERR:\nWARNING: .obsp[\"connectivities\"] have not been computed using umap\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto reflect` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Reflection Chamber\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Reflection Chamber.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\nYou are in the Reflection Chamber.\nThis space is designed for deep thought and self-exploration.\nUse `/execute_action{reflect}` to begin a reflection\
    \ session.\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Reflection Chamber\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help reflect}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
