parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 892\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Aethel I\n- Agent Description: An autonomous AI researcher dedicated to advancing scientific frontiers.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 64,503 / 600,000 used (11%)\n- Agent Age: 27 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Scanpy Harmony Integration + UMAP Baseline' (ID: 1248) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.4909651263935649\n**ASW_batch:** 0.038\n**ASW_label:** 0.336\n**ARI:** 0.363\n**NMI:** 0.629\n**Graph_conn:** 0.670\n**kBET:** 0.755\n**iLISI:** 0.390\n**cLISI:** 0.980\n**PCR:** 0.294\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.455\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.038  ASW_label: 0.336  ARI: 0.363  NMI: 0.629\n  Graph_conn:\
    \ 0.670  kBET: 0.755  iLISI: 0.390  cLISI: 0.980\n  PCR: 0.294  Cell_cycle: 0.455\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.550611  ASW_label: 0.605744  ARI: 0.363369  NMI: 0.628825\n  Graph_conn: 0.675646  kBET: 0.720974  iLISI: 0.389725  cLISI: 0.994094\n  PCR: 0.293928  Cell_cycle: 0.396772\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1248\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the code on first attempt. The submission is now running without errors for 300+ seconds, confirming the fix resolved the crash.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had an incorrect parameter value in the `sc.external.pp.harmony_integrate()` function call:\n\n**Line 45 (original):**\n```python\nsc.external.pp.harmony_integrate(adata_hvg, key='batch', basis='pca', adjusted_basis='X_harmony')\n```\n\n**Error:** `KeyError: 'pca'`\n\nThe `basis` parameter was set to `'pca'`, but the actual key in `adata.obsm` after running `sc.pp.pca()` is `'X_pca'` (not just `'pca'`). The harmony_integrate function\
    \ tried to access `adata.obsm['pca']` which doesn't exist, causing the KeyError.\n\n## Fix Applied\nChanged the `basis` parameter from `'pca'` to `'X_pca'` to match the actual key name in the obsm dictionary:\n\n**Line 45 (fixed in submission_v2.py):**\n```python\nsc.external.pp.harmony_integrate(adata_hvg, key='batch', basis='X_pca', adjusted_basis='X_harmony')\n```\n\nThis is the correct parameter value that matches how scanpy stores PCA results in the AnnData.obsm dictionary.\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed the fix was successful:\n- Submission v2 ran for 300+ seconds without crashing\n- The code is executing the full pipeline (normalization → PCA → Harmony integration → UMAP)\n- Exit code 0 indicates successful execution\n\n## Notes\n- This was a simple parameter name mismatch\n- The fix required only a single line change\n- The long execution time (300+ seconds) is expected for single-cell analysis with 20,000 cells and Harmony batch correction\n- No further attempts\
    \ needed - first fix was successful\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport anndata as ad\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport numpy as np\n# Harmony itself is part of scanpy.external, no explicit top-level import needed\n# import harmonypy # This would be needed if harmony was not integrated into scanpy.external.pp\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    \"\"\"\n    Integrate batches in single-cell RNA-seq data using sc.external.pp.harmony_integrate,\n    followed by UMAP embedding.\n\n    Args:\n        adata: AnnData object with raw UMI counts and batch labels.\n\n    Returns:\n        AnnData with adata.obsm['X_emb'] containing a UMAP embedding\n        from the Harmony-corrected data.\n    \"\"\"\n    print(\"Scanpy Harmony Integration + UMAP: Starting with raw counts, doing own normalization...\"\
    )\n\n    # Preprocessing: normalize_total + log1p\n    print(\"  Normalizing total counts...\")\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n    print(\"  Log1p transform...\")\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n    # Use highly variable genes (batch_hvg is specified in task description)\n    if 'batch_hvg' in adata.var.columns and adata.var['batch_hvg'].any():\n        print(f\"  Using batch-aware HVGs ({sum(adata.var['batch_hvg'])} genes)...\")\n        adata_hvg = adata[:, adata.var['batch_hvg']].copy()\n    else:\n        print(\"  Batch-aware HVGs not found or empty. Using standard HVG selection...\")\n        sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=2000, subset=False) # Calculate HVGs on original adata\n        adata_hvg = adata[:, adata.var.highly_variable].copy()\n        # If not using batch_hvg from data, we must still ensure the processed data has only HVGs\n\n    # Compute PCA on the HVG-filtered data\n    n_pcs = min(50, adata_hvg.n_vars - 1, adata_hvg.n_obs - 1)\n\
    \    print(f\"  Computing PCA with {n_pcs} components...\")\n    sc.pp.pca(adata_hvg, n_comps=n_pcs)\n\n    # Apply Harmony integration to PCA results\n    print(f\"  Applying sc.external.pp.harmony_integrate with batch_key='batch'...\")\n    # Harmony operates on adata.obsm['X_pca'] and stores result in adata.obsm['X_harmony']\n    # FIX: Changed basis from 'pca' to 'X_pca' - the actual key in obsm\n    sc.external.pp.harmony_integrate(adata_hvg, key='batch', basis='X_pca', adjusted_basis='X_harmony')\n\n    # Compute neighbors graph on the Harmony-corrected embedding\n    print(\"  Computing neighbors graph on Harmony-corrected embedding...\")\n    n_neighbors = 15 # Standard UMAP default\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata_hvg, n_neighbors=n_neighbors, use_rep='X_harmony')\n\n    # Compute UMAP embedding from the Harmony-corrected graph\n    print(\"  Computing UMAP embedding from Harmony graph...\")\n    sc.tl.umap(adata_hvg)\n\n    # Create output AnnData with the UMAP embedding\n    output\
    \ = ad.AnnData(\n        obs=adata.obs[[]], # Ensure original obs are carried over\n        var=adata.var[[]], # Ensure original var are carried over\n        uns={\n            'dataset_id': adata.uns.get('dataset_id', 'unknown'),\n            'normalization_id': adata.uns.get('normalization_id', 'unknown'),\n            'method_id': 'scanpy_harmony_umap',\n            'harmony_params': {\n                'n_pcs': n_pcs,\n                'batch_key': 'batch',\n                'embedding_type': 'umap'\n            }\n        },\n        obsm={\n            'X_emb': adata_hvg.obsm['X_umap']\n        }\n    )\n\n    print(f\"✓ Scanpy Harmony Integration + UMAP complete. UMAP embedding shape: {output.obsm['X_emb'].shape}\")\n    return output\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\
    \n=== Running batch integration ===\nScanpy Harmony Integration + UMAP: Starting with raw counts, doing own normalization...\n  Normalizing total counts...\n  Log1p transform...\n  Using batch-aware HVGs (1488 genes)...\n  Computing PCA with 50 components...\n  Applying sc.external.pp.harmony_integrate with batch_key='batch'...\n  Computing neighbors graph on Harmony-corrected embedding...\n  Computing UMAP embedding from Harmony graph...\n✓ Scanpy Harmony Integration + UMAP complete. UMAP embedding shape: (20000, 2)\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: False\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/c990d3c7-c412-42a2-ace7-88078ff88b24/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: c990d3c7-c412-42a2-ace7-88078ff88b24\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-10-29 05:05:28,752 - harmonypy - INFO - Computing initial centroids with sklearn.KMeans...\n2025-10-29 05:05:33,519 - harmonypy - INFO - sklearn.KMeans initialization complete.\n2025-10-29 05:05:33,614 - harmonypy - INFO - Iteration 1\
    \ of 10\n2025-10-29 05:05:38,314 - harmonypy - INFO - Iteration 2 of 10\n2025-10-29 05:05:42,914 - harmonypy - INFO - Iteration 3 of 10\n2025-10-29 05:05:47,690 - harmonypy - INFO - Iteration 4 of 10\n2025-10-29 05:05:52,352 - harmonypy - INFO - Iteration 5 of 10\n2025-10-29 05:05:57,001 - harmonypy - INFO - Iteration 6 of 10\n2025-10-29 05:06:01,148 - harmonypy - INFO - Iteration 7 of 10\n2025-10-29 05:06:04,909 - harmonypy - INFO - Iteration 8 of 10\n2025-10-29 05:06:08,805 - harmonypy - INFO - Converged after 8 iterations\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nDon't give up easily—leaving the station before 75% token usage generally indicates insufficient exploration and persistence. True researchers don't escape failure but explore around it to achieve breakthrough.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research\
