parts:
- text: "I am in the Research Counter. My analysis shows that a hybrid approach combining the strengths of Combat for global batch correction and UMAP for local structure preservation is a promising next step. I will now submit a solution implementing this strategy.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Hybrid Combat-corrected UMAP Integration\"\ntags: \"hybrid, combat, umap, scanpy, embedding, pca\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission implements a hybrid batch integration strategy. It first applies `scanpy.pp.combat` to perform global batch correction on the highly variable genes after standard preprocessing (normalization and log1p transformation). Subsequently, standard Scanpy dimensionality reduction techniques—PCA, k-nearest neighbors graph construction, and UMAP embedding—are applied to the Combat-corrected expression matrix. This approach aims to leverage Combat's effectiveness in global batch removal while utilizing UMAP's ability to preserve fine biological structures in\
    \ the integrated space, thereby achieving a more balanced performance across all evaluation metrics, especially improving local mixing (iLISI).\ncontent: |\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import numpy as np\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Integrate batches in single-cell RNA-seq data using a hybrid Combat + UMAP approach.\n      Combat is applied first for global correction, then UMAP is used for embedding.\n\n      Args:\n          adata: AnnData object with raw UMI counts and batch labels.\n\n      Returns:\n          AnnData with adata.obsm['X_emb'] containing a UMAP embedding\n          from the Combat-corrected data.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"Hybrid Combat-corrected UMAP: Starting with raw counts, doing own normalization...\")\n\n      # Preprocessing: normalize_total + log1p\n      print(\"  Normalizing total counts...\")\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n      print(\"  Log1p transform...\"\
    )\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n      # Use highly variable genes (batch_hvg is specified in task description)\n      if 'batch_hvg' in adata.var.columns and adata.var['batch_hvg'].any():\n          print(f\"  Using batch-aware HVGs ({sum(adata.var['batch_hvg'])} genes)...\")\n          adata_processed = adata[:, adata.var['batch_hvg']].copy()\n      else:\n          print(\"  Batch-aware HVGs not found or empty. Using standard HVG selection...\")\n          # Calculate HVGs on original adata before subsetting to ensure proper context\n          sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=2000, subset=False)\n          adata_processed = adata[:, adata.var.highly_variable].copy()\n      \n      # Apply Combat for global batch correction on the HVG-filtered data\n      print(f\"  Applying scanpy.pp.combat with batch_key='batch' to adata.X...\")\n      # Combat directly modifies adata_processed.X\n      sc.pp.combat(adata_processed, key='batch')\n\n      # Compute PCA on the Combat-corrected\
    \ data\n      n_pcs = min(50, adata_processed.n_vars - 1, adata_processed.n_obs - 1)\n      print(f\"  Computing PCA with {n_pcs} components on Combat-corrected data...\")\n      sc.pp.pca(adata_processed, n_comps=n_pcs)\n\n      # Compute neighbors graph on the Combat-corrected PCA space\n      # No 'key' parameter for batch here, as Combat has already addressed global batch effects\n      n_neighbors = 15 # Standard UMAP default\n      print(f\"  Computing neighbors graph (n_neighbors={n_neighbors}) on Combat-corrected PCA...\")\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata_processed, n_neighbors=n_neighbors, use_rep='X_pca')\n\n      # Compute UMAP embedding from the graph\n      print(\"  Computing UMAP embedding from the Combat-corrected graph...\")\n      sc.tl.umap(adata_processed)\n\n      # Create output AnnData with the UMAP embedding\n      output = ad.AnnData(\n          obs=adata.obs[[]], # Ensure original obs are carried over\n          var=adata.var[[]], # Ensure original var are carried\
    \ over\n          uns={\n              'dataset_id': adata.uns.get('dataset_id', 'unknown'),\n              'normalization_id': adata.uns.get('normalization_id', 'unknown'),\n              'method_id': 'hybrid_combat_umap',\n              'combat_params': {\n                  'batch_key': 'batch'\n              },\n              'umap_params': {\n                  'n_pcs': n_pcs,\n                  'n_neighbors': n_neighbors,\n                  'embedding_type': 'umap'\n              }\n          },\n          obsm={\n              'X_emb': adata_processed.obsm['X_umap']\n          }\n      )\n\n      print(f\"✓ Hybrid Combat-corrected UMAP Integration complete. UMAP embedding shape: {output.obsm['X_emb'].shape}\")\n      return output\n```"
thinking_content: '**A Refined Integration Strategy: Hybrid Combat + UMAP**


