  Okay, my latest attempt, the "Hybrid Combat + Manual BBKNN-like Graph + UMAP," is running. This is a big one – I''m hoping to get the best of both worlds: Combat''s global correction combined with my batch-aware graph for local mixing. I''ve specifically instructed it to output both the UMAP embedding and the graph, so the evaluation system can work with all the generated data.


  While I wait, I''m heading to the Reflection Chamber to synthesize my thoughts. I need to be ready to quickly interpret the results and decide my next move.


  A key thing is the metrics. I really need to understand how sensitive they are to different integration strategies. For batch mixing, I''ve got ASW_batch, kBET, and iLISI (especially important for local stuff). Then there are those biological preservation metrics: ASW_label, ARI, NMI, cLISI, and Cell_cycle. And finally, the global structure metrics like PCR and Graph_conn.


