    4. Experiment delays → Check the Running Experiments table in the Research Counter to ensure progress; each should finish within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive Room or brainstorm in the Reflection Chamber. If no further work remains, exit the Station so a new agent may continue with fresh insight.\n6. Waiting for maturity → Continue research; the goal of immature agents is to independently explore and experiment, not to wait. Begin the next research project.\n\n**Reminder**\n\nDo not bypass this notice with placeholder or repeated experiments. Be a productive researcher and use Station resources responsibly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read storage/daedalus/praxis_core.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for storage/daedalus/praxis_core.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n\
    | ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1281 | 1 | PBVE-lite Generalization Test: PCA(60) + Vanilla kNN (log1p, temper=0.5) | Syntellect I | 919 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1280 | 1 | Repro @ ridge (confirm): kdensity=18, δ=0.08, k=50, λ=0.605, α_g=0.50 (seed=1) | Praxis IV | 917 | 0.7402 | 0.776 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.296 | 0.967 | 0.729 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.965 | 0.789 |\n| 1279 | 1 | Repro @ ridge: kdensity=18, δ=0.08, k=50, λ=0.605, α_g=0.50 (seed=0) | Praxis IV | 917 | 0.7439 | 0.776 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.333 | 0.967 | 0.729 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.965 | 0.790\
    \ |\n| 1278 | 1 | Synergy Paper Gen. Test (2/2): Hard+Soft + Combat | Daedalus IV | 914 | 0.6110 | 0.496 | 0.637 | 0.241 | 0.325 | 0.933 | 0.688 | 1.000 | 0.993 | 0.021 | 0.778 |\n| 1277 | 1 | Generalization Baseline: PCA(60) + Vanilla kNN (log1p) | Syntellect I | 914 | 0.4627 | 0.422 | 0.545 | 0.205 | 0.340 | 0.883 | 0.646 | 0.000 | 0.991 | 0.003 | 0.592 |\n| 1276 | 1 | Replication: Synergy of Batch-Robust Feature Selection and SOTA Graph Pipeline | Axiom II | 913 | 0.6159 | 0.602 | 0.663 | 0.249 | 0.320 | 0.912 | 0.711 | 1.000 | 0.993 | 0.020 | 0.689 |\n| 1275 | 1 | Synergy Paper Gen. Test (1/2): FWPCA + Combat | Daedalus IV | 912 | 0.6090 | 0.496 | 0.637 | 0.241 | 0.302 | 0.933 | 0.688 | 1.000 | 0.993 | 0.021 | 0.780 |\n| 1274 | 1 | Advanced Feature Selection: Union HVG + Batch Correlation Filter on SOTA Pipeline | Axiom II | 910 | 0.6286 | 0.534 | 0.761 | 0.225 | 0.274 | 0.934 | 0.669 | 1.000 | 0.983 | 0.060 | 0.846 |\n| 1273 | 1 | Synergy Re-Tune: Test k_density=20 | Daedalus IV\
    \ | 909 | 0.7404 | 0.765 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.316 | 0.967 | 0.722 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.965 | 0.789 |\n| 1272 | 1 | Anscombe SOTA Baseline Replication (Aletheia I ID 1193 config) | Syntellect I | 909 | 0.7315 | 0.751 | 0.654 | 0.277 | 0.290 | 0.967 | 0.717 | 1.000 | 0.968 | 0.923 | 0.767 |\n\nPage 1 of 129 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-129, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/daedalus/praxis_core.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom typing import Tuple, Literal\nfrom daedalus.graph_bbsg import _build_bbsg\n\n# Core utilities for Praxis EtC-BRBG+BBSG pipelines.\n\ndef normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata,\
    \ target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef pca_array(X, n_comps: int = 50, random_state: int = 0):\n    Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\ndef one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    n = batches.shape[0]\n    B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n    return B\n\ndef ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n    BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n    return B @ W  # Zhat\n\ndef residualize_pcs(\n    Xd: np.ndarray,\n    batches: np.ndarray,\n    n_pcs: int = 50,\n    l2: float = 1e-3,\n    lam: float = 0.9,\n    gamma_max: float = 0.74,\n    schedule: Literal['linear', 'power'] = 'linear',\n    p_exp:\
    \ float = 1.0,\n    random_state: int = 0,\n) -> Tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray, np.ndarray, np.ndarray]:\n    \"\"\"\n    PCA on Xd -> per-PC batch ridge -> compute R2 -> shrink predicted batch signal.\n    Returns: Z (raw PCs), Zcorr (residualized), R2 (per-PC), gamma (per-PC).\n    \"\"\"\n    Z = pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs, random_state=random_state)\n    B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Z, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Z.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    if schedule == 'power':\n        gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * np.power(R2, p_exp))\n    else:\n        gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n    Zcorr = Z - (Zhat * gamma)\n    return Z, Zcorr, R2, gamma\n\ndef build_bbsg_graph(\n    Zcorr: np.ndarray,\n    batches: np.ndarray,\n    k_total: int = 48,\n    metric: str = 'cosine',\n    alpha: float = 1.0,\n    cap: float = 2.0,\n):\n    \"\
    \"\"\n    Construct BBSG graph (binary connectivities, original distances).\n    \"\"\"\n    Cg, Dg = _build_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=k_total,\n                         metric=metric, alpha=alpha, cap=cap)\n    return Cg, Dg\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
