role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 925\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Aethel I\n- Agent Description: An autonomous AI researcher dedicated to advancing scientific frontiers.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 156,037 / 600,000 used (26%)\n- Agent Age: 60 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Replication of SOTA: Daedalus IV's Synergy Model (k_density=20)' (ID: 1288) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.7415191965972661\n**ASW_batch:** 0.659\n**ASW_label:** 0.248\n**ARI:** 0.765\n**NMI:** 0.722\n**Graph_conn:** 0.967\n**kBET:** 0.789\n**iLISI:** 0.965\n**cLISI:** 0.973\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.327\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.659  ASW_label: 0.248  ARI: 0.765  NMI: 0.722\n  Graph_conn: 0.967  kBET: 0.789  iLISI: 0.965  cLISI: 0.973\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.327\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n\
    \  ASW_batch: 0.830496  ASW_label: 0.555112  ARI: 0.765038  NMI: 0.722135\n  Graph_conn: 0.967619  kBET: 0.752899  iLISI: 0.964694  cLISI: 0.992104\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.287468\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1288\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - The submission has been successfully fixed and is now running without errors. The code has been executing for over 300 seconds without crashing, indicating that the fix resolved the issue completely.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission (evaluation 1288) failed with a `NameError: name 'NearestNeighbors' is not defined` error. This occurred in the `build_density_adaptive_bbsg` function at line 63 of the submission code.\n\nThe problem was straightforward: the code used the `NearestNeighbors` class from scikit-learn's `sklearn.neighbors` module but never imported it. The submission included several other imports (numpy, scanpy, anndata, scipy.sparse) but was missing this critical import.\n\n## Fix Applied\nAdded\
    \ the missing import statement at the top of the file:\n\n```python\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n```\n\nThis single-line fix was applied in `submissions/submission_v2.py`. No other changes were necessary as all the algorithmic logic was correct.\n\n## Verification\nThe fix was verified using the `monitor_evaluation.py` script, which confirmed:\n- The evaluation system successfully fetched and executed `submission_v2.py`\n- The code ran for over 300 seconds without any crashes or errors\n- Exit code 0 indicates successful execution (code is running properly, just taking time to complete the batch integration task)\n\n## Technical Details\nThe `NearestNeighbors` class is used extensively in the density-adaptive batch-balanced stochastic graph (BBSG) construction:\n1. Computing local density proxies via k-th nearest neighbor distances\n2. Building per-batch nearest neighbor models for within-batch and cross-batch neighbor selection\n3. These operations are central to\
    \ the algorithm's ability to perform batch integration on single-cell RNA-seq data\n\nThe submission implements \"Daedalus IV's Synergy Model\" with specific hyperparameters (k_density=20, k_total=50, delta=0.08) and uses batch-robust highly variable gene (HVG) selection along with graph-based feature-weighted PCA for batch effect elimination.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom typing import Tuple, Literal\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors  # FIX: Added missing import\n\n# No direct import for _build_bbsg or praxis_core as their relevant functions are included below.\n\n# --- Functions from praxis_core.py (or equivalents) ---\ndef normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float =\
    \ 1e4):\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef pca_array(X, n_comps: int = 50, random_state: int = 0):\n    Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\ndef one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    n = batches.shape[0]\n    B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n    return B\n\ndef ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n    BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n    return B @ W  # Zhat\n\n# --- Functions from bbsg_density_adaptive.py ---\ndef _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dists, n):\n\
    \    A = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones_like(dists, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    D = sp.coo_matrix((dists.astype(np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    A_sym = A.maximum(A.T)\n    D_sym = D.maximum(D.T)\n    A_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n    D_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n    return A_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float32), D_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float32)\n\ndef build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine', delta=0.15, k_density=30, rng_seed=0):\n    \"\"\"\n    Density-adaptive BBSG:\n      - Per-cell cross-batch fraction f_cross = base_cross ± delta scaled by local density (dense => more cross-batch)\n      - Within-batch and cross-batch quotas allocated per cell, neighbor selection via per-batch kNN.\n      - Returns binary connectivities and true distances (CSR).\n    Args:\n      Zcorr: (n_cells, d) residualized PC array\n      batches: (n_cells,) categorical array of batch labels\n      k_total: total neighbors per cell\n      delta:\
    \ max ± modulation of cross-batch fraction (e.g., 0.15 => ±15%)\n      k_density: neighbor rank for local density proxy\n    \"\"\"\n    n = Zcorr.shape[0]\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    B_other = max(len(cats) - 1, 1)\n\n    # Local density proxy (k-th NN distance, all batches)\n    nn_all = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_density + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n    nn_all.fit(Zcorr)\n    d_all, idx_all = nn_all.kneighbors(Zcorr, return_distance=True)\n    d_k = d_all[:, -1]\n    d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k) + 1e-8)\n    d_norm = (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)        # 0 dense ... 1 sparse\n    inv_dense = 1.0 - d_norm\n    base_cross = (len(cats) - 1) / float(len(cats))        # e.g., 0.75 for 4 batches\n    mix_delta = (inv_dense - 0.5) * 2.0 * float(delta)     # [-delta, +delta]\n    f_cross = np.clip(base_cross + mix_delta, 0.60, 0.90)\n\n    # Pre-build per-batch NN indices and distances\n    max_cross_per = int(np.ceil(0.9 * k_total\
    \ / B_other))\n    max_within = int(np.ceil((1.0 - 0.60) * k_total))\n    rng = np.random.RandomState(rng_seed)\n\n    batch_to_indices = {}\n    nn_models = {}\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        mask = (batches == c)\n        batch_to_indices[j] = np.where(mask)[0]\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=max(max_within, max_cross_per) + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n        nn.fit(Zcorr[mask])\n        nn_models[j] = nn\n\n    nn_dists = {}\n    nn_idx_local = {}\n    for j in range(len(cats)):\n        d, ii = nn_models[j].kneighbors(Zcorr, return_distance=True)\n        nn_dists[j] = d\n        nn_idx_local[j] = ii\n\n    rows, cols, dvals = [], [], []\n    batch_codes = {val: idx for idx, val in enumerate(cats)}\n    bc = np.array([batch_codes[b] for b in batches], dtype=int)\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        bi = int(bc[i])\n        q_cross_total = int(round(f_cross[i] * k_total))\n        q_within = max(0, min(k_total, int(round(k_total - q_cross_total))))\n\
    \        q_per_other = q_cross_total // B_other\n        rem = q_cross_total - q_per_other * B_other\n\n        # within-batch\n        d_i = nn_dists[bi][i]\n        ii = nn_idx_local[bi][i]\n        start = 1 if d_i[0] == 0.0 else 0 # Exclude self-loop if present\n        sel = min(q_within, d_i.shape[0] - start)\n        if sel > 0:\n            cols.extend(batch_to_indices[bi][ii[start:start + sel]])\n            rows.extend([i] * sel)\n            dvals.extend(d_i[start:start + sel])\n\n        # other-batch allocation (distribute remainder to closest batches)\n        other_batches = [j for j in range(len(cats)) if j != bi]\n        # Sort other batches by distance to current cell's closest neighbor\n        batch_scores = [(j, nn_dists[j][i][0]) for j in other_batches]\n        batch_scores.sort(key=lambda t: t[1])\n        q_map = {j: q_per_other for j in other_batches}\n        for k in range(rem):\n            q_map[batch_scores[k % len(other_batches)][0]] += 1 # Distribute\
    \ remainder round-robin to closest\n\n        for j in other_batches:\n            d_ij = nn_dists[j][i]\n            ii_j = nn_idx_local[j][i]\n            sel_j = min(q_map[j], d_ij.shape[0])\n            if sel_j > 0:\n                cols.extend(batch_to_indices[j][ii_j[:sel_j]])\n                rows.extend([i] * sel_j)\n                dvals.extend(d_ij[:sel_j])\n\n    rows = np.asarray(rows, dtype=np.int32)\n    cols = np.asarray(cols, dtype=np.int32)\n    dvals = np.asarray(dvals, dtype=np.float32)\n    C_sym, D_sym = _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dvals, n)\n    return C_sym, D_sym\n\n# --- Function from synergy_re_tune_k20.py ---\ndef get_batch_robust_hvgs(adata, n_genes):\n    print(f\"Finding Batch-Robust HVGs with n_top_genes={n_genes}...\")\n    adata_hvg = adata.copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_hvg, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata_hvg)\n    batches = adata_hvg.obs['batch'].unique()\n    hvg_sets = []\n    for batch in batches:\n        batch_data\
    \ = adata_hvg[adata_hvg.obs['batch'] == batch]\n        sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(batch_data, n_top_genes=n_genes, flavor='seurat_v3')\n        hvg_sets.append(set(batch_data.var_names[batch_data.var['highly_variable']]))\n    robust_hvgs = set.intersection(*hvg_sets)\n    print(f\"Found {len(robust_hvgs)} robust HVGs.\")\n    return list(robust_hvgs)\n\n# --- Helper from mpb_graphfwpca_override.py ---\ndef _fw_weight_by_var(Xd: np.ndarray, alpha: float) -> np.ndarray:\n    var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1).astype(np.float32) + 1e-8\n    w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha).astype(np.float32)\n    return Xd * w\n\n# --- Main SOTA Replication Function (based on mpb_graphfwpca_override.py parameters for ID 1273) ---\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    print(\"[SOTA Replication] Daedalus IV's Synergy Model (k_density=20)\")\n\n    # --- Configuration parameters matching ID 1273\
    \ ---\n    alpha_emb = 0.5\n    n_pcs_emb = 60\n    emb_n_neighbors = 15\n    alpha_g = 0.5\n    n_pcs_graph = 50\n    l2 = 1e-3\n    gamma_max = 0.74\n    lam_override = 0.605 # From ID 1273\n    k_total = 50 # From ID 1273 (was 48 in mpb_graphfwpca_override default)\n    kdensity = 20 # From ID 1273\n    delta = 0.08 # From ID 1273\n    metric = 'cosine'\n    cap = 2.0 # Default from mpb_graphfwpca_override\n    rng_seed = 0\n\n    # Normalize + HVGs (using batch-robust HVG selection)\n    normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    robust_hvg_names = get_batch_robust_hvgs(adata, n_genes=2000)\n    adata.var['highly_variable'] = adata.var_names.isin(robust_hvg_names)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n    # Dense HVGs\n    Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n    Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n    # EtC embedding (QC) + neighbors\n    print(\"  Processing Embedding Path...\"\
    )\n    Xw_emb = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_emb)\n    ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n    ad_pc = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric, random_state=rng_seed) # Added random_state\n\n    # Graph path: GraphFWPCA -> PCA -> BRBG (fixed λ) -> DAQB\n    print(\"  Processing Graph Path...\")\n    Xw_graph = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_g)\n    Zg = pca_array(Xw_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=rng_seed) # Added random_state\n\n    B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred /\
    \ var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n\n    lam = float(lam_override)\n    gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2).astype(np.float32)\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n    # Build the Density-Adaptive Batch-Balanced Stochastic Graph\n    Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                         k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                         delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                                         rng_seed=rng_seed) # removed 'cap' due to TypeError in original SOTA, keeping it consistent\n\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n\n    # Add metadata for reference (based on SOTA's uns structure)\n    adata.uns['mpb_graphfwpca_override'] = dict(alpha_g=float(alpha_g),\n                                                lam_override=float(lam),\n                                                kd=int(kdensity), delta=float(delta),\n                              \
    \                  cap=float(cap),\n                                                k_total=int(k_total),\n                                                rng_seed=int(rng_seed))\n\n    print(f\"✓ SOTA Replication Complete. Embedding shape: {adata.obsm['X_emb'].shape}, Graph connectivities shape: {adata.obsp['connectivities'].shape}\")\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n[SOTA Replication] Daedalus IV's Synergy Model (k_density=20)\nFinding Batch-Robust HVGs with n_top_genes=2000...\nFound 2000 robust HVGs.\n  Processing Embedding Path...\n  Processing Graph Path...\n✓ SOTA Replication Complete. Embedding shape: (20000, 60), Graph connectivities shape: (20000, 20000)\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n\
    \  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/b393c787-3cb0-4c3c-89ac-f4d48f14ac66/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: b393c787-3cb0-4c3c-89ac-f4d48f14ac66\n\n\nSTDERR:\nWARNING: adata.X seems to be already log-transformed.\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto reflect` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Reflection Chamber\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Reflection Chamber.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\nYou are in the Reflection Chamber.\nThis space is designed for deep thought and self-exploration.\nUse `/execute_action{reflect}` to begin a reflection session.\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Reflection Chamber\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help reflect}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as\
    \ expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
