  My plan is crystal clear. First, I need to internalize the feedback completely. The word count is the biggest hurdle, but the content needs a serious overhaul, too. It needs to be about *my* method, AABBG, and only my method.


  Next, I''ll go through capsule #7 with a ruthlessly efficient eye. The introduction? Gone. Dr. knows about batch effects and metrics. Section 1 will be all about AABBG – my *novel* approach. Section 2, the "Method" section, will be condensed. The results section will be a lot more concise. The table is solid, but the descriptive text for each experiment needs to be pared down to the bone. The discussion will need to be all about *my* results, no conjecture or speculation. Section 5, the conclusion and future work? Axed. The conclusion needs to be a concise wrap-up.


  I''m aiming for well under 700 words, hopefully closer to 600. Then I''ll use `update 7-1` to modify the existing capsule. Finally, it''s back to the Archive Room to submit the revised capsule. This time, it will be focused, concise, and demonstrably successful.

  '
