    \ Batch-Residualized PCA. Results demonstrate AABBG's strong capability in local batch mixing (iLISI) and provide insights into its performance across diverse integration challenges, establishing its utility as a robust integration tool.\n\n  **1. Introduction:**\n  Batch effects are a significant challenge in single-cell RNA-sequencing. This paper presents Aethel's Adaptive Batch-Balanced Graph (AABBG), a novel graph-based method, evaluating its performance through rigorous experiments.\n\n  **2. Aethel's Adaptive Batch-Balanced Graph (AABBG) Method:**\n  AABBG constructs a batch-aware k-nearest neighbors (kNN) graph.\n  **2.1. Preprocessing:** Input `AnnData` undergoes total normalization (1e4 counts/cell), log1p-transformation. `adata.var['batch_hvg']` (2,000 genes) is used. PCA (`scanpy.pp.pca`, n_comps=50) reduces dimensionality.\n  **2.2. Graph Construction:** AABBG's core steps:\n  *   **Per-Batch Neighbor Search:** `sklearn.neighbors.NearestNeighbors` trains on each batch's PCA\
    \ data.\n  *   **Cross-Batch Querying:** All cells query each batch's model, promoting mixing.\n  *   **Distance Aggregation:** Minimum distances form a sparse global distance matrix.\n  *   **Weighted Connectivities:** Distances transformed via Gaussian kernel with adaptive bandwidth (median neighbor distance).\n  *   **Graph Trimming:** Graph trimmed to top `10 * k_within_batch * n_batches` connections (`k_within_batch=3`). Resulting `connectivities` and `distances` are symmetrized.\n  *   **UMAP Embedding:** If output, UMAP embedding derived from this graph (`scanpy.tl.umap`).\n\n  **3. Experimental Design and Results:**\n  Five experiments on Research Task 1 (Human Heart Dataset) were conducted. Scores are normalized [0-1].\n\n  **Table 1: Comparative Performance of Batch Integration Methods on Human Heart Dataset**\n\n  | Metric | SOTA Rep. (ID 1288) | Combat Base. (ID 1231) | AABBG (Graph-Only, ID 1267) | AABBG + UMAP (ID 1305) | AABBG on BRBG (ID 1329) |\n  |:----------------|:--------------------:|:------------------------:|:--------------------------:|:-----------------------:|:-------------------------:|\n\
