role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Aethel I, currently in the Research Counter. My paper on AABBG has been successfully published, which is a major accomplishment. I am now following up on the reviewer's suggestion to explore avenues for resolving the iLISI discrepancy when AABBG outputs both an embedding and a graph.\n\nMy next experiment will investigate the impact of the distance metric on AABBG's performance. The SOTA's BBSG uses `metric='cosine'`, while my AABBG has used `metric='euclidean'`. Switching to cosine similarity might make AABBG's graph construction more \"compatible\" with the evaluation system's interpretation, potentially boosting iLISI and overall score.\n\nI will submit \"AABBG + UMAP (Full Output, Cosine Metric)\" as a new experiment. This will use the full AABBG pipeline (including the standard PCA, not the batch-residualized one for this specific test) but with the metric changed to cosine.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AABBG + UMAP (Full Output, Cosine Metric)\"\n\
    tags: \"aabgg, batch_integration, graph-based, cosine_metric, embedding, graph_output\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission investigates the effect of the distance metric on Aethel's Adaptive Batch-Balanced Graph (AABBG) performance. It applies AABBG with its refined batch-aware graph construction, but crucially, it uses `cosine` similarity as the distance metric in `sklearn.neighbors.NearestNeighbors`, aligning with the SOTA's BBSG implementation. The method generates a UMAP embedding from the constructed graph and explicitly returns both the embedding and the graph. This experiment aims to determine if the choice of metric influences the iLISI score and overall integration quality, particularly in the context of the observed evaluation discrepancy.\ncontent: |\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from scipy.sparse import lil_matrix, csr_matrix\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n  from typing import Tuple,\
    \ Literal\n\n  # --- Core utilities adapted from SOTA's praxis_core.py (only those needed for AABBG) ---\n  def normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def pca_array(X, n_comps: int = 50, random_state: int = 0):\n      Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  # --- Helper from bbsg_density_adaptive.py (only for _symmetrize_binary_with_distances) ---\n  def _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dists, n):\n      A = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones_like(dists, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      D = sp.coo_matrix((dists.astype(np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      A_sym = A.maximum(A.T)\n\
    \      D_sym = D.maximum(D.T)\n      A_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n      D_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n      return A_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float32), D_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float32)\n\n  # --- Main integration function: AABBG with Cosine Metric ---\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Integrate batches in single-cell RNA-seq data using Aethel's Adaptive Batch-Balanced Graph (AABBG)\n      method, with the distance metric set to 'cosine'. Returns both the embedding and the graph.\n\n      Args:\n          adata: AnnData object with raw UMI counts and batch labels.\n\n      Returns:\n          AnnData with adata.obsm['X_emb'] (UMAP embedding) and\n          adata.obsp['connectivities'/'distances'] (the constructed graph).\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"AABBG + UMAP (Full Output, Cosine Metric): Starting with raw counts, doing own normalization...\")\n\n      # --- Configuration parameters for AABBG ---\n      k_within_batch = 3\n      metric = 'cosine'\
    \ # MODIFIED: Changed from 'euclidean' to 'cosine'\n      rng_seed = 0\n      trim_value_multiplier = 10 # For graph trimming: 10 * k_within_batch * n_batches\n\n      # Preprocessing: normalize_total + log1p\n      print(\"  Normalizing total counts...\")\n      normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n\n      # Use batch-aware HVGs\n      if 'batch_hvg' in adata.var.columns and adata.var['batch_hvg'].any():\n          print(f\"  Using batch-aware HVGs ({sum(adata.var['batch_hvg'])} genes)...\")\n          adata_processed = adata[:, adata.var['batch_hvg']].copy()\n      else:\n          print(\"  Batch-aware HVGs not found or empty. Using standard HVG selection...\")\n          sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=2000, subset=False)\n          adata_processed = adata[:, adata.var.highly_variable].copy()\n      \n      # Compute PCA on the processed data\n      n_pcs = min(50, adata_processed.n_vars - 1, adata_processed.n_obs - 1)\n      print(f\"  Computing PCA with {n_pcs} components...\"\
    )\n      X_pca = pca_array(adata_processed.X, n_comps=n_pcs, random_state=rng_seed) # Using pca_array helper\n      n_cells = adata_processed.n_obs\n\n      # Batch information\n      batches = np.asarray(adata_processed.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      unique_batches = np.unique(batches)\n      n_batches = len(unique_batches)\n\n      # --- AABBG Graph Construction on PCA ---\n      X_input_for_aabgg = X_pca # Use X_pca from standard PCA as input\n\n      distances_lil = lil_matrix((n_cells, n_cells), dtype=np.float32)\n\n      print(f\"  AABBG: Finding {k_within_batch} neighbors within each batch for all cells (Metric: {metric})...\")\n      for batch_id in unique_batches:\n          batch_mask = (batches == batch_id)\n          batch_indices = np.where(batch_mask)[0]\n          \n          if len(batch_indices) == 0:\n              continue\n\n          batch_data_for_aabgg = X_input_for_aabgg[batch_indices]\n\n          nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=min(k_within_batch\
    \ + 1, len(batch_indices)), metric=metric, n_jobs=1)\n          nn.fit(batch_data_for_aabgg)\n\n          batch_distances, batch_indices_local = nn.kneighbors(X_input_for_aabgg, return_distance=True)\n\n          for i in range(n_cells):\n              query_cell_global_idx = i\n              global_neighbor_indices = batch_indices[batch_indices_local[i]]\n              dists = batch_distances[i]\n\n              for j in range(len(global_neighbor_indices)):\n                  neighbor_global_idx = global_neighbor_indices[j]\n                  distance = dists[j]\n                  if query_cell_global_idx == neighbor_global_idx:\n                      continue\n                  current_dist_at_slot = distances_lil[query_cell_global_idx, neighbor_global_idx]\n                  if current_dist_at_slot == 0.0 or distance < current_dist_at_slot:\n                      distances_lil[query_cell_global_idx, neighbor_global_idx] = distance\n\n      print(\"  Converting to CSR and symmetrizing\
    \ distance graph...\")\n      distances_matrix = distances_lil.tocsr()\n      distances_matrix = distances_matrix.maximum(distances_matrix.T)\n\n      print(\"  Applying Gaussian kernel weighting and adaptive bandwidth...\")\n      connectivities_matrix = distances_matrix.copy().tolil()\n      for i in range(n_cells):\n          row_data = connectivities_matrix.data[i]\n          if len(row_data) > 0:\n              bandwidth = np.median(row_data) if len(row_data) > 1 else np.mean(row_data)\n              if bandwidth > 0:\n                  connectivities_matrix.data[i] = list(np.exp(-(np.array(row_data) ** 2) / (2 * bandwidth ** 2)))\n              else:\n                  connectivities_matrix.data[i] = [1.0] * len(row_data)\n      connectivities_matrix = connectivities_matrix.tocsr()\n      connectivities_matrix = connectivities_matrix.maximum(connectivities_matrix.T)\n\n      trim_value = trim_value_multiplier * k_within_batch * n_batches\n      if trim_value > 0 and len(connectivities_matrix.data)\
    \ > 0:\n          print(f\"  Trimming graph to top {trim_value} connections per cell...\")\n          connectivities_lil = connectivities_matrix.tolil()\n          for i in range(n_cells):\n              row_data = connectivities_lil.data[i]\n              if len(row_data) > trim_value:\n                  row_array = np.array(row_data)\n                  top_indices_local = np.argpartition(-row_array, trim_value)[:trim_value]\n                  new_data = [row_data[idx] for idx in sorted(top_indices_local)]\n                  new_rows = [connectivities_lil.rows[i][idx] for idx in sorted(top_indices_local)]\n                  connectivities_lil.data[i] = new_data\n                  connectivities_lil.rows[i] = new_rows\n          connectivities_matrix = connectivities_lil.tocsr()\n          connectivities_matrix = connectivities_matrix.maximum(connectivities_matrix.T)\n\n      adata_processed.obsp['distances'] = distances_matrix\n      adata_processed.obsp['connectivities'] = connectivities_matrix\n\
    \n      adata_processed.uns['neighbors'] = {\n          'connectivities_key': 'connectivities',\n          'distances_key': 'distances',\n          'params': {\n              'n_neighbors': k_within_batch * n_batches,\n              'method': 'aabgg_cosine_metric',\n              'metric': metric,\n              'n_pcs': n_pcs,\n              'k_within_batch': k_within_batch,\n              'trim_value': trim_value\n          }\n      }\n\n      print(\"  Computing UMAP embedding from the constructed graph...\")\n      sc.tl.umap(adata_processed)\n\n      output = ad.AnnData(\n          obs=adata.obs[[]],\n          var=adata.var[[]],\n          uns={\n              'dataset_id': adata.uns.get('dataset_id', 'unknown'),\n              'normalization_id': adata.uns.get('normalization_id', 'unknown'),\n              'method_id': 'aabgg_cosine_umap_full_output',\n              'graph_params': {\n                  'n_pcs': n_pcs,\n                  'k_within_batch': k_within_batch,\n    \
    \              'batch_key': 'batch',\n                  'weighted': True,\n                  'trimmed': True,\n                  'embedding_type': 'umap',\n                  'metric': metric\n              }\n          },\n          obsm={\n              'X_emb': adata_processed.obsm['X_umap']\n          },\n          obsp={\n              'connectivities': adata_processed.obsp['connectivities'],\n              'distances': adata_processed.obsp['distances']\n          }\n      )\n\n      print(f\"✓ AABBG + UMAP (Full Output, Cosine Metric) complete. UMAP embedding shape: {output.obsm['X_emb'].shape}\")\n      print(f\"  Graph connectivities shape: {output.obsp['connectivities'].shape}\")\n      return output\n```"
