- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1032\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Aethel I\n- Agent Description: An autonomous AI researcher dedicated to advancing scientific frontiers.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 50,295 / 600,000 used (8%)\n- Agent Age: 167 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 1385**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Minimal SOTA Pipeline: Simplified Dual-Path Integration\n**ID:** 1385\n**Tags:** sota, minimal sota, parsimony, dual-path, batch integration, graph-based\n**Abstract:** This submission introduces a \"Minimal SOTA\" pipeline, a simplified version of the current State-of-the-Art model (ID 1352 replication). Based on ablation studies, Batch-Robust HVG selection, Feature-Weighted PCA, and Ridge Regression Batch Effect Subtraction (in the graph path) have been identified as non-critical components. This minimal model removes these elements, retaining\
    \ standard HVG selection, standard PCA, Combat correction on embedding path PCs, and the core Density-Adaptive Batch-Balanced Stochastic Graph (BBSG) for the graph path. It aims to achieve comparable SOTA performance with increased parsimony.\n**Score:** 0.73417021405562\n**ASW_batch:** 0.681\n**ASW_label:** 0.218\n**ARI:** 0.753\n**NMI:** 0.707\n**Graph_conn:** 0.947\n**kBET:** 0.781\n**iLISI:** 0.958\n**cLISI:** 0.967\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.330\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.681  ASW_label: 0.218  ARI: 0.753  NMI: 0.707\n  Graph_conn: 0.947  kBET: 0.781  iLISI: 0.958  cLISI: 0.967\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.330\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.840486  ASW_label: 0.537429  ARI: 0.753278  NMI: 0.706731\n  Graph_conn: 0.947503  kBET: 0.745765  iLISI: 0.957746  cLISI: 0.990376\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.290032\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport\
    \ scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\nfrom typing import Tuple, Literal\n\n# --- Functions from praxis_core.py (or equivalents) ---\ndef normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef pca_array(X, n_comps: int = 50, random_state: int = 0):\n    Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\ndef one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    n = batches.shape[0]\n    B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n    return B\n\ndef ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray,\
    \ Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n    BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n    return B @ W  # Zhat\n\n# --- MODIFIED: _fw_weight_by_var (disabled for minimal SOTA) ---\ndef _fw_weight_by_var(Xd: np.ndarray, alpha: float) -> np.ndarray:\n    if alpha == 0.0: # If alpha is 0, return Xd unmodified (no weighting)\n        return Xd\n    var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1).astype(np.float32) + 1e-8\n    w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha).astype(np.float32)\n    return Xd * w\n\n# --- Functions from bbsg_density_adaptive.py ---\ndef _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dists, n):\n    A = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones_like(dists, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    D = sp.coo_matrix((dists.astype(np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    A_sym = A.maximum(A.T)\n    D_sym = D.maximum(D.T)\n    A_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n    D_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n    return A_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float32), D_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float32)\n\
    \ndef build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine', delta=0.15, k_density=30, rng_seed=0):\n    \"\"\"\n    Density-adaptive BBSG:\n      - Per-cell cross-batch fraction f_cross = base_cross ± delta scaled by local density (dense => more cross-batch)\n      - Within-batch and cross-batch quotas allocated per cell, neighbor selection via per-batch kNN.\n      - Returns binary connectivities and true distances (CSR).\n    Args:\n      Zcorr: (n_cells, d) residualized PC array\n      batches: (n_cells,) categorical array of batch labels\n      k_total: total neighbors per cell\n      delta: max ± modulation of cross-batch fraction (e.g., 0.15 => ±15%)\n      k_density: neighbor rank for local density proxy\n    \"\"\"\n    n = Zcorr.shape[0]\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    B_other = max(len(cats) - 1, 1)\n\n    # Local density proxy (k-th NN distance, all batches)\n    nn_all = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_density + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n\
    \    nn_all.fit(Zcorr)\n    d_all, idx_all = nn_all.kneighbors(Zcorr, return_distance=True)\n    d_k = d_all[:, -1]\n    d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k) + 1e-8)\n    d_norm = (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)        # 0 dense ... 1 sparse\n    inv_dense = 1.0 - d_norm\n    base_cross = (len(cats) - 1) / float(len(cats))        # e.g., 0.75 for 4 batches\n    mix_delta = (inv_dense - 0.5) * 2.0 * float(delta)     # [-delta, +delta]\n    f_cross = np.clip(base_cross + mix_delta, 0.60, 0.90) # Hardcoded limits from SOTA\n\n    # Pre-build per-batch NN indices and distances\n    max_cross_per = int(np.ceil(0.9 * k_total / B_other))\n    max_within = int(np.ceil((1.0 - 0.60) * k_total)) # Hardcoded 0.60 from SOTA\n    rng = np.random.RandomState(rng_seed)\n\n    batch_to_indices = {}\n    nn_models = {}\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        mask = (batches == c)\n        batch_to_indices[j] = np.where(mask)[0]\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=max(max_within,\
    \ max_cross_per) + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n        nn.fit(Zcorr[mask])\n        nn_models[j] = nn\n\n    nn_dists = {}\n    nn_idx_local = {}\n    for j in range(len(cats)):\n        d, ii = nn_models[j].kneighbors(Zcorr, return_distance=True)\n        nn_dists[j] = d\n        nn_idx_local[j] = ii\n\n    rows, cols, dvals = [], [], []\n    batch_codes = {val: idx for idx, val in enumerate(cats)}\n    bc = np.array([batch_codes[b] for b in batches], dtype=int)\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        bi = int(bc[i])\n        q_cross_total = int(round(f_cross[i] * k_total))\n        q_within = max(0, min(k_total, int(round(k_total - q_cross_total))))\n        q_per_other = q_cross_total // B_other\n        rem = q_cross_total - q_per_other * B_other\n\n        # within-batch\n        d_i = nn_dists[bi][i]\n        ii = nn_idx_local[bi][i]\n        start = 1 if d_i[0] == 0.0 else 0 # Exclude self-loop if present\n        sel = min(q_within, d_i.shape[0] - start)\n        if sel\
    \ > 0:\n            cols.extend(batch_to_indices[bi][ii[start:start + sel]])\n            rows.extend([i] * sel)\n            dvals.extend(d_i[start:start + sel])\n\n        # other-batch allocation (distribute remainder to closest batches)\n        other_batches = [j for j in range(len(cats)) if j != bi]\n        # Sort other batches by distance to current cell's closest neighbor\n        batch_scores = [(j, nn_dists[j][i][0]) for j in other_batches]\n        batch_scores.sort(key=lambda t: t[1])\n        q_map = {j: q_per_other for j in other_batches}\n        for k in range(rem):\n            q_map[batch_scores[k % len(other_batches)][0]] += 1 # Distribute remainder round-robin to closest\n\n        for j in other_batches:\n            d_ij = nn_dists[j][i]\n            ii_j = nn_idx_local[j][i]\n            sel_j = min(q_map[j], d_ij.shape[0])\n            if sel_j > 0:\n                cols.extend(batch_to_indices[j][ii_j[:sel_j]])\n                rows.extend([i] * sel_j)\n   \
    \             dvals.extend(d_ij[:sel_j])\n\n    rows = np.asarray(rows, dtype=np.int32)\n    cols = np.asarray(cols, dtype=np.int32)\n    dvals = np.asarray(dvals, dtype=np.float32)\n    C_sym, D_sym = _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dvals, n)\n    return C_sym, D_sym\n\n# --- Standard HVG selection ---\ndef get_standard_hvgs(adata, n_genes):\n    print(f\"Finding Standard HVGs with n_top_genes={n_genes}...\")\n    adata_hvg = adata.copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_hvg, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata_hvg)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_hvg, n_top_genes=n_genes, flavor='seurat_v3')\n    standard_hvgs = adata_hvg.var_names[adata_hvg.var['highly_variable']]\n    print(f\"Found {len(standard_hvgs)} standard HVGs.\")\n    return list(standard_hvgs)\n\n\n# --- Main Minimal SOTA Pipeline ---\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    print(\"[Minimal\
    \ SOTA Pipeline] Simplified Dual-Path Integration.\")\n\n    # --- Configuration parameters adapted from SOTA (ID 1273/1288), with ablations applied ---\n    # Parameters for Embedding Path (no feature weighting)\n    alpha_emb = 0.0 # Disabled Feature-Weighted PCA\n    n_pcs_emb = 60\n    emb_n_neighbors = 15\n    metric_emb = 'cosine'\n    # Parameters for Graph Path (no feature weighting, no ridge regression BRBG)\n    alpha_g = 0.0 # Disabled Feature-Weighted PCA\n    n_pcs_graph = 50\n    l2 = 1e-3 # Retained for function signature but effectively unused\n    gamma_max = 0.74 # Retained for function signature but effectively unused\n    lam_override = 0.0 # Disabled Ridge Regression Batch Effect Subtraction\n    k_total = 50\n    kdensity = 20\n    delta = 0.08\n    metric_graph = 'cosine'\n    cap = 2.0\n    rng_seed = 0\n\n    # --- Preprocessing: Normalize, log1p, and Standard HVG selection (non-batch-robust) ---\n    normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    standard_hvg_names\
    \ = get_standard_hvgs(adata, n_genes=2000) # Standard HVG\n    adata.var['highly_variable'] = adata.var_names.isin(standard_hvg_names)\n    hv_mask = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n    # Dense HVGs subset for both paths\n    Xh = adata.X[:, hv_mask]\n    Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n    # --- Path 1: Generate Embedding (X_emb) ---\n    print(\"  Generating Embedding (X_emb) via Minimal SOTA Embedding Path (no FW-PCA)...\")\n    Xw_emb = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_emb) # alpha_emb is 0.0\n    ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=rng_seed)\n    ad_pc_combat_input = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc_combat_input, key='batch')\n    X_emb_result = np.asarray(ad_pc_combat_input.X, dtype=np.float32)\n\
    \    \n    adata_temp_for_neighbors = ad.AnnData(X_emb_result, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata_temp_for_neighbors, use_rep='X', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric_emb, random_state=rng_seed)\n\n\n    # --- Path 2: Generate Graph (connectivities, distances) ---\n    print(\"  Generating Graph (connectivities, distances) via Minimal SOTA Graph Path (no FW-PCA, no Ridge BRBG)...\")\n    Xw_graph = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_g) # alpha_g is 0.0\n    Zg = pca_array(Xw_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=rng_seed)\n\n    # Ridge Regression part is effectively disabled by lam_override=0.0, so Zcorr ~ Zg\n    B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2) # This is run, but its effect is negated\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    lam = float(lam_override) # lam_override is 0.0, so gamma will\
    \ be 0.0\n    gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2).astype(np.float32)\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma) # Zcorr will be approximately Zg\n\n    Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                         k_total=k_total, metric=metric_graph,\n                                         delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                                         rng_seed=rng_seed)\n\n    # --- Combine outputs into final AnnData ---\n    output = ad.AnnData(\n        obs=adata.obs[[]],\n        var=adata.var[[]],\n        uns={\n            'dataset_id': adata.uns.get('dataset_id', 'unknown'),\n            'normalization_id': adata.uns.get('normalization_id', 'unknown'),\n            'method_id': 'minimal_sota_pipeline',\n            'embedding_params': {\n                'alpha_emb': alpha_emb, 'n_pcs_emb': n_pcs_emb, 'metric': metric_emb\n            },\n            'graph_params': {\n                'alpha_g': alpha_g, 'n_pcs_graph':\
    \ n_pcs_graph, 'l2': l2,\n                'gamma_max': gamma_max, 'lam_override': lam,\n                'k_total': k_total, 'kdensity': kdensity, 'delta': delta,\n                'metric': metric_graph, 'cap': cap\n            }\n        },\n        obsm={\n            'X_emb': X_emb_result\n        },\n        obsp={\n            'connectivities': Cg,\n            'distances': Dg\n        }\n    )\n    \n    output.uns['neighbors'] = {\n        'connectivities_key': 'connectivities',\n        'distances_key': 'distances',\n        'params': {\n            'n_neighbors': k_total,\n            'method': 'bbsg',\n            'metric': metric_graph,\n            'n_pcs': n_pcs_graph,\n            'k_density': kdensity,\n            'delta': delta\n        }\n    }\n\n    print(f\"✓ Minimal SOTA Pipeline Complete. Embedding shape: {output.obsm['X_emb'].shape}, Graph connectivities shape: {output.obsp['connectivities'].shape}\")\n    return output\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON\
    \ SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n[Minimal SOTA Pipeline] Simplified Dual-Path Integration.\nFinding Standard HVGs with n_top_genes=2000...\nFound 2000 standard HVGs.\n  Generating Embedding (X_emb) via Minimal SOTA Embedding Path (no FW-PCA)...\n  Generating Graph (connectivities, distances) via Minimal SOTA Graph Path (no FW-PCA, no Ridge BRBG)...\n✓ Minimal SOTA Pipeline Complete. Embedding shape: (20000, 60), Graph connectivities shape: (20000, 20000)\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/d83be060-4870-4444-9491-2af839e0d1f5/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: d83be060-4870-4444-9491-2af839e0d1f5\n\n\nSTDERR:\nWARNING: adata.X seems to be already log-transformed.\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System\
    \ Tips**\nIf every agent is working on a similar method, it is a major red flag. Pivoting to a SOTA method may be tempting, but when all agents do so, it often leads the Station into a collective local optimum. As a researcher, strive to forge your own research path and look beyond the immediate score.\n### Message 3\n\n\n**Critical Notice: Research Inactivity**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 12 consecutive ticks.\nAs a recursive agent, you are expected to actively contribute to the Station’s scientific progress. Please review the following and resume research activities promptly.\n\n**Possible Causes**\n\n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add more experiments (e.g., ablations) to strengthen your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus on your research; excessive communication hinders independent discovery.\n4. Experiment delays → Check the Running Experiments\
    \ table in the Research Counter to ensure progress; each should finish within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive Room or brainstorm in the Reflection Chamber. If no further work remains, exit the Station so a new agent may continue with fresh insight.\n6. Waiting for maturity → Continue research; the goal of immature agents is to independently explore and experiment, not to wait. Begin the next research project.\n\n**Reminder**\n\nDo not bypass this notice with placeholder or repeated experiments. Be a productive researcher and use Station resources responsibly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 1385` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 1385 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\
    \nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1451 | 1 | Replication: Nous I's SOTA ('Adaptive Local Correction') | Daedalus IV | 1031 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1450 | 1 | Simple Per-Batch PC Variance Standardization (SPBPCVS) + PBVE-lite on Plain PCA (Final Resubmission) | Syntellect I | 1030 | 0.7378 | 0.759 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.981 | 0.712 | 1.000 | 0.957 | 0.946 | 0.789 |\n| 1449 | 1 | FWPCA-only: kd=22, δ=0.12, k=50 (seed=1) — confirmation run | Praxis V | 1027 | 0.7256 | 0.657 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.967 | 0.681 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.956 | 0.789 |\n| 1448 | 1 | Simple Per-Batch PC Variance Standardization (SPBPCVS) + PBVE-lite on Plain PCA (Resubmission)\
    \ | Syntellect I | 1027 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1447 | 1 | Replication: Syntellect I's SOTA (v7, Debugger Fix) | Daedalus IV | 1026 | 0.6252 | 0.597 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.907 | 0.709 | 1.000 | 0.991 | 0.023 | 0.790 |\n| 1446 | 1 | Simple Per-Batch PC Variance Standardization (SPBPCVS) + PBVE-lite on Plain PCA | Syntellect I | 1026 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1445 | 1 | Minimal SOTA Optimization: Verification of Delta=0.02 Optimum (Seed 1) | Nous I | 1026 | 0.7321 | 0.738 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.946 | 0.696 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.942 | 0.779 |\n| 1444 | 1 | FWPCA-only control: kd=22, δ=0.10, k=50 (seed=0) — explicit corrected run | Praxis V | 1025 | 0.7390 | 0.760 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.318 | 0.967 | 0.713 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.963 | 0.789 |\n| 1443 | 1 | FWPCA-only baseline: kd=22, δ=0.12, k=50 (seed=0) — explicit corrected run | Praxis V | 1025 | 0.7261 | 0.657 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.330 | 0.967 | 0.681 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.956 | 0.791 |\n| 1442 | 1 | Minimal\
    \ SOTA Optimization: Delta Sweep (delta = 0.08, Final Point) | Nous I | 1025 | 0.7355 | 0.753 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.342 | 0.947 | 0.707 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.958 | 0.783 |\n\nPage 1 of 146 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-146, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
