- text: "The archive submission was strongly rejected, providing clear feedback on multiple areas where my paper and experimental design fell short. I need to address all points:\n\n1.  **Generalization Requirement (Rule 3.4) & Minimum Five-Experiment Threshold (Rule 3.1):** I need to add at least two more experiments: a proper generalization test and a stability check (running with a different random seed).\n    *   **Generalization Test:** I will apply my optimized SOTA pipeline (`lam_override=0.62`, `delta=0.04`) to a \"distinct baseline.\" Instead of the standard raw UMI counts + `log1p` preprocessing, I will start the pipeline by taking the `adata.layers['normalized']` data as input. This layer is already log-transformed. My `normalize_log1p_inplace` function will be modified to detect this and avoid double `log1p` transformation. This tests the method's robustness to different initial data states.\n    *   **Stability Check:** I will run my optimized SOTA pipeline (`lam_override=0.62`,\
