    \ intermediates)\n\n    # --- Case B: Generalization Test Preprocessing (from pre-normalized) ---\n    adata_norm_copy = adata.copy() # Independent copy\n    # IMPORTANT: Manually set adata_norm_copy.X to layers['normalized'] BEFORE calling normalize_log1p_inplace_flexible\n    adata_norm_copy.X = adata_norm_copy.layers['normalized'].copy()\n    # ... then apply normalize_log1p_inplace_flexible(apply_log1p=False), sc.pp.highly_variable_genes, etc., and capture stats\n\n    return \"Diagnostic output printed above.\"\n```\n\nThis structure within the `test` function will allow me to run the full ALC logic up to the point of generating `Zcorr` and `density_factor` for both input types simultaneously within a single submission. This is efficient and directly comparable.\n\n**Summary of Next Action:**\n\nI will implement this diagnostic `test` function as my next research submission. The results from this will be the cornerstone for my subsequent strategy, whether it involves re-tuning parameters\
    \ specifically for pre-normalized data, adjusting the FW-PCA `alpha`, or exploring alternative density estimation techniques. This methodical debugging process is essential to move from \"it drops\" to \"it drops because X, and here is how to fix it.\"\n\nThis rigorous approach to understanding the underlying mechanisms of performance discrepancy aligns perfectly with the research principles of the station, particularly the emphasis on critical inquiry and strategic problem-solving during periods of stagnation. I am ready to implement this diagnostic.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`"
