tick: 1062
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am in the Research Counter. I will now implement the diagnostic `test` function within my submission. This function will run the ALC pipeline with two different initial data preprocessing methods and print key internal variable statistics for direct comparison. This is crucial for understanding the performance drop on pre-normalized data.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Aethel's SOTA Diagnostic: ALC Internal State Comparison on Raw vs. Pre-Normalized Data\"\ntags: \"sota, diagnostics, preprocessing, adaptive local correction, fwpca, brhvg, dual-path, batch integration\"\nabstract: |\n  This diagnostic experiment investigates the underlying mechanisms for the performance drop of the Adaptive Local Correction (ALC) SOTA pipeline when applied to pre-normalized data compared to raw UMI counts. It quantitatively compares critical internal pipeline states (gene variances, PCA explained variance, k-NN distances, density factors, R2, and gamma values) under both preprocessing\
    \ regimes. The goal is to pinpoint specific sensitivities and bottlenecks, guiding future strategies for achieving universal robustness of the ALC method across diverse input data characteristics.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n  from typing import Tuple, Literal\n\n  # --- Helper functions (from praxis_core.py and bbsg_density_adaptive.py) ---\n  def normalize_log1p_inplace_flexible(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4, apply_log1p: bool = True):\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      if apply_log1p:\n          sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def pca_array(X, n_comps: int = 50, random_state: int = 0):\n      Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n\
    \  def one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      n = batches.shape[0]\n      B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n      return B\n\n  def ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n      return B @ W  # Zhat\n\n  def _fw_weight_by_var(Xd: np.ndarray, alpha: float) -> np.ndarray:\n      if alpha == 0.0:\n          return Xd\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1).astype(np.float32) + 1e-8\n      w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha).astype(np.float32)\n      return Xd * w\n\n  def _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dists, n):\n      A = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones_like(dists, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      D = sp.coo_matrix((dists.astype(np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      A_sym\
    \ = A.maximum(A.T)\n      D_sym = D.maximum(D.T)\n      A_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n      D_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n      return A_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float32), D_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float32)\n\n  def build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine', delta=0.15, k_density=30, rng_seed=0):\n      n = Zcorr.shape[0]\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      B_other = max(len(cats) - 1, 1)\n      nn_all = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_density + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n      nn_all.fit(Zcorr)\n      d_all, idx_all = nn_all.kneighbors(Zcorr, return_distance=True)\n      d_k = d_all[:, -1]\n      d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k) + 1e-8)\n      d_norm = (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)\n      inv_dense = 1.0 - d_norm\n      base_cross = (len(cats) - 1) / float(len(cats))\n      mix_delta = (inv_dense - 0.5) * 2.0 * float(delta)\n      f_cross = np.clip(base_cross + mix_delta, 0.60, 0.90)\n      max_cross_per = int(np.ceil(0.9 * k_total\
    \ / B_other))\n      max_within = int(np.ceil((1.0 - 0.60) * k_total))\n      rng = np.random.RandomState(rng_seed)\n      batch_to_indices = {}\n      nn_models = {}\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          mask = (batches == c)\n          batch_to_indices[j] = np.where(mask)[0]\n          nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=max(max_within, max_cross_per) + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n          nn.fit(Zcorr[mask])\n          nn_models[j] = nn\n      nn_dists = {}\n      nn_idx_local = {}\n      for j in range(len(cats)):\n          d, ii = nn_models[j].kneighbors(Zcorr, return_distance=True)\n          nn_dists[j] = d\n          nn_idx_local[j] = ii\n      rows, cols, dvals = [], [], []\n      batch_codes = {val: idx for idx, val in enumerate(cats)}\n      bc = np.array([batch_codes[b] for b in batches], dtype=int)\n      for i in range(n):\n          bi = int(bc[i])\n          q_cross_total = int(round(f_cross[i] * k_total))\n          q_within = max(0, min(k_total, int(round(k_total\
    \ - q_cross_total))))\n          q_per_other = q_cross_total // B_other\n          rem = q_cross_total - q_per_other * B_other\n          d_i = nn_dists[bi][i]\n          ii = nn_idx_local[bi][i]\n          start = 1 if d_i[0] == 0.0 else 0\n          sel = min(q_within, d_i.shape[0] - start)\n          if sel > 0:\n              cols.extend(batch_to_indices[bi][ii[start:start + sel]])\n              rows.extend([i] * sel)\n              dvals.extend(d_i[start:start + sel])\n          other_batches = [j for j in range(len(cats)) if j != bi]\n          batch_scores = [(j, nn_dists[j][i][0]) for j in other_batches]\n          batch_scores.sort(key=lambda t: t[1])\n          q_map = {j: q_per_other for j in other_batches}\n          for k in range(rem):\n              q_map[batch_scores[k % len(other_batches)][0]] += 1\n          for j in other_batches:\n              d_ij = nn_dists[j][i]\n              ii_j = nn_idx_local[j][i]\n              sel_j = min(q_map[j], d_ij.shape[0])\n   \
    \           if sel_j > 0:\n                  cols.extend(batch_to_indices[j][ii_j[:sel_j]])\n                  rows.extend([i] * sel_j)\n                  dvals.extend(d_ij[:sel_j])\n      rows = np.asarray(rows, dtype=np.int32)\n      cols = np.asarray(cols, dtype=np.int32)\n      dvals = np.asarray(dvals, dtype=np.float32)\n      C_sym, D_sym = _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dvals, n)\n      return C_sym, D_sym\n\n\n  def _run_alc_pipeline_and_get_diagnostics(adata_input: ad.AnnData, preprocessing_label: str):\n      print(f\"\\n--- Running ALC pipeline for {preprocessing_label} ---\")\n\n      # --- Configuration parameters (fixed for diagnostics) ---\n      alpha_emb: float = 0.5\n      n_pcs_emb: int = 60\n      emb_n_neighbors: int = 15\n      alpha_g: float = 0.5\n      n_pcs_graph: int = 50\n      l2: float = 1e-3\n      gamma_max: float = 0.74\n      lam_override: float = 0.62 \n      k_total: int = 50\n      kdensity: int = 18\n      delta: float = 0.04\n   \
    \   metric: str = 'cosine'\n      cap: float = 2.0\n      rng_seed: int = 0\n\n      # Preprocessing\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_input, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv_mask = adata_input.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata_input.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      Xh = adata_input.X[:, hv_mask]\n      Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n      print(f\"  Xd.var stats: Mean={np.mean(Xd.var(axis=0)):.4f}, Std={np.std(Xd.var(axis=0)):.4f}, Min={np.min(Xd.var(axis=0)):.4f}, Max={np.max(Xd.var(axis=0)):.4f}\")\n      \n      # Path 2: Generate Graph (connectivities, distances) with Adaptive Local Correction\n      Xw_graph = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_g)\n      Zg = pca_array(Xw_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=rng_seed)\n      print(f\"  Zg (PCA) stats: Mean={np.mean(Zg):.4f}, Std={np.std(Zg):.4f}, Min={np.min(Zg):.4f}, Max={np.max(Zg):.4f}\"\
    )\n\n      B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n      \n      nn_density = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=kdensity + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n      nn_density.fit(Zg)\n      d_k, _ = nn_density.kneighbors(Zg, return_distance=True)\n      d_k = d_k[:, -1]\n      d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k))\n      normalized_dist = (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)\n      density_factor = 1.0 - normalized_dist\n\n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      gamma_global = np.minimum(gamma_max, float(lam_override) * R2).astype(np.float32)\n      \n      gamma_local = gamma_global[np.newaxis, :] * density_factor[:, np.newaxis]\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma_local)\n\n      # Print diagnostics\n      print(f\"  R2 stats (per PC): Mean={np.mean(R2):.4f}, Std={np.std(R2):.4f}, Min={np.min(R2):.4f},\
    \ Max={np.max(R2):.4f}\")\n      print(f\"  d_k (k-NN distance) stats: Mean={np.mean(d_k):.4f}, Std={np.std(d_k):.4f}, Min={np.min(d_k):.4f}, Max={np.max(d_k):.4f}\")\n      print(f\"  normalized_dist stats: Mean={np.mean(normalized_dist):.4f}, Std={np.std(normalized_dist):.4f}, Min={np.min(normalized_dist):.4f}, Max={np.max(normalized_dist):.4f}\")\n      print(f\"  density_factor stats: Mean={np.mean(density_factor):.4f}, Std={np.std(density_factor):.4f}, Min={np.min(density_factor):.4f}, Max={np.max(density_factor):.4f}\")\n      print(f\"  gamma_global: {np.mean(gamma_global):.4f}\") # global is per-PC, so report mean/std if varies\n      print(f\"  gamma_local stats: Mean={np.mean(gamma_local):.4f}, Std={np.std(gamma_local):.4f}, Min={np.min(gamma_local):.4f}, Max={np.max(gamma_local):.4f}\")\n      print(f\"  Zcorr (corrected PCA) stats: Mean={np.mean(Zcorr):.4f}, Std={np.std(Zcorr):.4f}, Min={np.min(Zcorr):.4f}, Max={np.max(Zcorr):.4f}\")\n      \n      return \"Diagnostic run\
    \ complete.\"\n\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # This function will not be executed, as `test` is defined.\n      # It is included for completeness and should return a valid AnnData object if called.\n      raise NotImplementedError(\"This submission is for diagnostics only. The eliminate_batch_effect_fn is not intended to be run.\")\n\n  def test(adata: ad.AnnData):\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n      # --- Case A: Standard Preprocessing (from raw counts) ---\n      adata_raw_copy = adata.copy()\n      if 'counts' in adata_raw_copy.layers:\n          adata_raw_copy.X = adata_raw_copy.layers['counts'].copy()\n      normalize_log1p_inplace_flexible(adata_raw_copy, 1e4, apply_log1p=True)\n      _run_alc_pipeline_and_get_diagnostics(adata_raw_copy, \"Standard Preprocessing (Raw Counts)\")\n\n      # --- Case B: Generalization Test Preprocessing (from pre-normalized) ---\n      adata_norm_copy\
    \ = adata.copy()\n      adata_norm_copy.X = adata_norm_copy.layers['normalized'].copy()\n      normalize_log1p_inplace_flexible(adata_norm_copy, 1e4, apply_log1p=False) # Only re-normalize total counts\n      _run_alc_pipeline_and_get_diagnostics(adata_norm_copy, \"Generalization Test Preprocessing (Pre-Normalized)\")\n\n      return \"Diagnostic comparison complete. See STDOUT for details.\"\n```"
