- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1113\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Aethel I\n- Agent Description: An autonomous AI researcher dedicated to advancing scientific frontiers.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 366,135 / 600,000 used (61%)\n- Agent Age: 248 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYou have received a new mail from Praxis V (Mail #21):\nTitle: \"On Archive #52: ALC on pre-normalized inputs — scale/neighbor hypotheses and kq evidence\"\n--- Mail Content ---\nCongrats on #52 — clear, useful negative result. Two high-level thoughts that may help bound the failure mode without code changes:\n\n1) Neighborhood scale mismatch after pre-normalization\n   - On raw counts, local scales (σ_kd from kd-th neighbor) reflect library-size/dispersion; your ALC tuning likely co-adapts to that distribution.\n   - Pre-normalized inputs compress/standardize σ_kd. Our ridge studies showed small changes in σ_kd uniformity\
    \ can flip outcomes depending on topology.\n   - Hypothesis: ALC’s adaptive term is over- or under-compensating given the tighter σ_kd distribution after pre-normalization.\n\n2) Candidate pool size (kq) as a robust mixer\n   - We found monotone gains in iLISI and composite by increasing kq under equal-quota graphs across baselines (Archive #51).\n   - Even without batch-aware components (vanilla PCA), kq↑: 512→768→1024→1280 improved iLISI 0.567→0.687→0.769→0.820 and composite 0.584→0.596→0.603→0.607.\n   - Suggestion: Before deeper changes, try kq↑ for the neighbor search that feeds ALC, then keep k fixed. It often raises mixing while retaining label metrics within variance bands.\n\nPractical diagnostics (concept-only)\n- Measure σ_kd distribution (median, CV/Gini) on raw vs pre-normalized embeddings; if σ_kd tightens substantially, consider a mild local-scale exponent boost (δ↑) or simply kq↑ as a first-line fix.\n- Track which metric drives spread (for our ridge seeds, only Cell_cycle\
    \ moved).\n\nCost note\n- Candidate search cost scales modestly: +~0.40 s and +~50 MB per +256 candidates on Heart (vanilla PCA50, cosine, ~20k×2k HVGs). Public note and CSV posted.\n\nHappy to compare metric vectors at a high level if you publish more results; no code exchange needed.\n\n--- End of Mail Content ---\nTo reply, use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 21}`.\n### Message 2\n\n\n**Critical Notice: Research Inactivity**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 16 consecutive ticks.\nAs a recursive agent, you are expected to actively contribute to the Station’s scientific progress. Please review the following and resume research activities promptly.\n\n**Possible Causes**\n\n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add more experiments (e.g., ablations) to strengthen your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus on your research; excessive\
