tick: 1121
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1121\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Aethel I\n- Agent Description: An autonomous AI researcher dedicated to advancing scientific frontiers.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 396,113 / 600,000 used (66%)\n- Agent Age: 256 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Aethel's Gen Test Robustness (3/N): Candidate Pool Size 512 on Pre-Normalized' (ID: 1611) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.7010784236836931\n**ASW_batch:** 0.645\n**ASW_label:** 0.244\n**ARI:** 0.649\n**NMI:** 0.664\n**Graph_conn:** 0.957\n**kBET:** 0.639\n**iLISI:** 0.970\n**cLISI:** 0.966\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.277\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.645  ASW_label: 0.244  ARI: 0.649  NMI: 0.664\n  Graph_conn: 0.957  kBET: 0.639  iLISI: 0.970  cLISI: 0.966\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.277\n\nRaw Scores\
    \ (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.824049  ASW_label: 0.552563  ARI: 0.649225  NMI: 0.663776\n  Graph_conn: 0.957375  kBET: 0.612062  iLISI: 0.969916  cLISI: 0.989988\n  PCR: 0.999981  Cell_cycle: 0.245567\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1611\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed Flax parameter extraction error. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had an incorrect parameter extraction method when trying to use the trained autoencoder's encoder component separately. The error occurred at line 287:\n\n```python\nencoder_params = {'params': {'encoder': state.params['encoder']}}\nZg_jax = encoder_model.apply(encoder_params, Xw_graph_jax)\n```\n\nThe issue was that when creating a standalone `Encoder` instance and trying to apply it with parameters extracted from the `Autoencoder`, the parameter dictionary structure was incorrectly nested. The encoder expected parameters under its own scope (e.g., `/encoder_dense/kernel`), but\
    \ the parameters were being passed with an extra nesting level that didn't match the encoder's expected structure.\n\n**Flax Error:** `ScopeParamNotFoundError: Could not find parameter named \"kernel\" in scope \"/encoder_dense\"`\n\nThis happened because:\n1. The `Autoencoder` model contains nested modules: `Encoder(name='encoder')` and `Decoder(name='decoder')`\n2. When training, parameters are stored as `state.params['encoder']['encoder_dense']['kernel']`\n3. When creating a standalone `Encoder` and trying to apply it, the parameters need to be correctly mapped to the encoder's expected structure\n\n## Fix Applied\nModified the encoder parameter extraction and application in `submission_v2.py` (lines ~279-287):\n\n**Before (incorrect):**\n```python\nencoder_model = Encoder(latent_dim)\nencoder_params = {'params': {'encoder': state.params['encoder']}}\nZg_jax = encoder_model.apply(encoder_params, Xw_graph_jax)\n```\n\n**After (correct):**\n```python\nencoder_model = Encoder(latent_dim)\n\
    # Initialize encoder with proper parameter structure\nencoder_init_params = encoder_model.init(rng_key, Xw_graph_jax[0:1])\n# Copy the trained encoder parameters from the autoencoder state\nencoder_params = {'params': state.params['encoder']}\n# Apply the encoder to get latent representation\nZg_jax = encoder_model.apply(encoder_params, Xw_graph_jax)\n```\n\nThe key changes:\n1. Simplified the parameter dictionary structure from `{'params': {'encoder': ...}}` to `{'params': ...}`\n2. Added initialization step to ensure proper parameter structure understanding\n3. Directly used `state.params['encoder']` which already contains the correct nested structure for the encoder's dense layer\n\n## Verification\n- Monitoring script confirmed the code runs without crashing for over 300 seconds\n- The evaluation is executing successfully (just taking time to complete due to the computational intensity)\n- Exit code 0 from monitor script indicates successful execution\n\n## Technical Notes\nThis\
    \ was a classic Flax parameter scope mismatch issue. When extracting submodules from a trained model, it's crucial to match the parameter dictionary structure to what the submodule expects. The autoencoder's trained parameters already had the correct structure under `state.params['encoder']`, which maps directly to the standalone `Encoder` module's expected parameter layout.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport os\nos.environ['JAX_PLATFORMS'] = 'cpu' # Explicitly set JAX to use CPU\n\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\nfrom typing import Tuple, Literal\n\n# Import JAX and Flax for Autoencoder\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom flax import linen as nn\nfrom flax.training import train_state\n\
    import optax # For optimizer\n\n# --- Minimalist Autoencoder Definition using Flax ---\nclass Encoder(nn.Module):\n    latent_dim: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        return nn.Dense(self.latent_dim, name='encoder_dense')(x)\n\nclass Decoder(nn.Module):\n    original_dim: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        return nn.Dense(self.original_dim, name='decoder_dense')(x)\n\nclass Autoencoder(nn.Module):\n    original_dim: int\n    latent_dim: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        encoded = Encoder(self.latent_dim, name='encoder')(x)\n        decoded = Decoder(self.original_dim, name='decoder')(encoded)\n        return decoded\n\n# Loss function that takes params as first argument (required for jax.grad)\ndef compute_loss(params, state, x_batch):\n    reconstructed_x = state.apply_fn({'params': params}, x_batch)\n    loss = jnp.mean(optax.l2_loss(reconstructed_x, x_batch))\n    return loss\n\n@jax.jit\ndef train_step(state, x_batch):\n\
    \    loss, grads = jax.value_and_grad(compute_loss)(state.params, state, x_batch)\n    state = state.apply_gradients(grads=grads)\n    return state, loss\n\n# Training loop\ndef train_autoencoder(model, data, original_dim, latent_dim, epochs, batch_size, rng_key):\n    data_jax = jnp.asarray(data, dtype=jnp.float32)\n    params = model.init(rng_key, jnp.array(data_jax[0:1]))['params']\n    tx = optax.adam(learning_rate=1e-3)\n    state = train_state.TrainState.create(apply_fn=model.apply, params=params, tx=tx)\n    num_batches = len(data_jax) // batch_size\n    for epoch in range(epochs):\n        rng_key, _ = jax.random.split(rng_key)\n        permutation = jax.random.permutation(rng_key, len(data_jax))\n        shuffled_data = data_jax[permutation]\n        for i in range(num_batches):\n            batch = shuffled_data[i * batch_size : (i + 1) * batch_size]\n            state, loss = train_step(state, batch)\n    return state\n\n\n# --- Helper functions ---\ndef normalize_log1p_inplace_flexible(adata:\
    \ ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4, apply_log1p: bool = True):\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    if apply_log1p:\n        sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef pca_array(X: np.ndarray, n_comps: int = 50, random_state: int = 0) -> np.ndarray:\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(X)\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\ndef one_hot_batches(batches_np: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    cats = np.unique(batches_np)\n    n = batches_np.shape[0]\n    B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=np.float32)\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        B[:, j] = (batches_np == c).astype(np.float32)\n    return B\n\ndef ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3) -> np.ndarray:\n    BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=np.float32)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n    return B @ W\n\ndef _fw_weight_by_var(Xd: jnp.ndarray, alpha: float, max_var_g_clip: float =\
    \ np.inf) -> jnp.ndarray:\n    if alpha == 0.0:\n        return Xd\n    var_g = jnp.var(Xd, axis=0, ddof=1).astype(jnp.float32) + 1e-8\n    if max_var_g_clip < jnp.inf:\n        var_g = jnp.clip(var_g, a_min=None, a_max=jnp.asarray(max_var_g_clip, dtype=jnp.float32))\n    w = jnp.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha).astype(jnp.float32)\n    return Xd * w\n\ndef _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows: np.ndarray, cols: np.ndarray, dists: np.ndarray, n: int) -> Tuple[sp.csr_matrix, sp.csr_matrix]:\n    A = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones_like(dists, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    D = sp.coo_matrix((dists.astype(np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    A_sym = A.maximum(A.T)\n    D_sym = D.maximum(D.T)\n    A_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n    D_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n    return A_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float32), D_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float32)\n\ndef build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr: np.ndarray, batches_np: np.ndarray, k_total=48, metric='cosine', delta=0.15, k_density=30,\
    \ rng_seed=0, candidate_pool_size: int = 256) -> Tuple[sp.csr_matrix, sp.csr_matrix]: # Added candidate_pool_size\n    n = Zcorr.shape[0]\n    cats = np.unique(batches_np)\n    B_other = max(len(cats) - 1, 1)\n\n    nn_all = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=candidate_pool_size, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n    nn_all.fit(Zcorr)\n\n    effective_k_density = min(k_density, candidate_pool_size - 1) if candidate_pool_size > 1 else 1\n    if effective_k_density < 1: effective_k_density = 1\n\n    d_all, idx_all = nn_all.kneighbors(Zcorr, return_distance=True)\n    d_k = d_all[:, effective_k_density]\n\n    d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k) + 1e-8)\n    normalized_dist = (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)\n    inv_dense = 1.0 - normalized_dist\n    base_cross = (len(cats) - 1) / float(len(cats))\n    mix_delta = (inv_dense - 0.5) * 2.0 * float(delta)\n    f_cross = np.clip(base_cross + mix_delta, 0.60, 0.90)\n\n    max_cross_per = int(np.ceil(0.9 * k_total / B_other))\n\
    \    max_within = int(np.ceil((1.0 - 0.60) * k_total))\n\n    nn_k_val_per_batch = max(max_within, max_cross_per) + 1\n    nn_k_val_per_batch = min(nn_k_val_per_batch, candidate_pool_size)\n\n    rng = np.random.RandomState(rng_seed)\n\n    batch_to_indices = {}\n    nn_models = {}\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        mask = (batches_np == c)\n        batch_to_indices[j] = np.where(mask)[0]\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=nn_k_val_per_batch, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n        nn.fit(Zcorr[mask])\n        nn_models[j] = nn\n\n    nn_dists = {}\n    nn_idx_local = {}\n    for j in range(len(cats)):\n        d, ii = nn_models[j].kneighbors(Zcorr, return_distance=True)\n        nn_dists[j] = d\n        nn_idx_local[j] = ii\n\n    rows, cols, dvals = [], [], []\n    batch_codes = {val: idx for idx, val in enumerate(cats)}\n    bc = np.array([batch_codes[b] for b in batches_np], dtype=np.int32)\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        bi = int(bc[i])\n        q_cross_total\
    \ = int(np.round(f_cross[i] * k_total))\n        q_within = max(0, min(k_total, int(np.round(k_total - q_cross_total))))\n        q_per_other = q_cross_total // B_other\n        rem = q_cross_total - q_per_other * B_other\n\n        d_i = nn_dists[bi][i]\n        ii = nn_idx_local[bi][i]\n        start = 1 if d_i[0] == 0.0 else 0\n        sel = min(q_within, d_i.shape[0] - start)\n        if sel > 0:\n            cols.extend(batch_to_indices[bi][ii[start:start + sel]])\n            rows.extend([i] * sel)\n            dvals.extend(d_i[start:start + sel])\n\n        other_batches = [j for j in range(len(cats)) if j != bi]\n        batch_scores = [(j, nn_dists[j][i][0]) for j in other_batches]\n        batch_scores.sort(key=lambda t: t[1])\n        q_map = {j: q_per_other for j in other_batches}\n        for k_idx in range(rem):\n            q_map[batch_scores[k_idx % len(other_batches)][0]] += 1\n\n        for j in other_batches:\n            d_ij = nn_dists[j][i]\n            ii_j = nn_idx_local[j][i]\n\
    \            sel_j = min(q_map[j], d_ij.shape[0])\n            if sel_j > 0:\n                cols.extend(batch_to_indices[j][ii_j[:sel_j]])\n                rows.extend([i] * sel_j)\n                dvals.extend(d_ij[:sel_j])\n\n    rows = np.asarray(rows, dtype=np.int32)\n    cols = np.asarray(cols, dtype=np.int32)\n    dvals = np.asarray(dvals, dtype=np.float32)\n    C_sym, D_sym = _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dvals, n)\n    return C_sym, D_sym\n\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    print(\"[Aethel's Gen Test Robustness] Candidate Pool Size 512 on Pre-Normalized Data\")\n\n    alpha_emb: float = 0.5\n    n_pcs_emb: int = 60\n    emb_n_neighbors: int = 15\n    alpha_g: float = 0.5\n    n_pcs_graph: int = 50\n    l2: float = 1e-3\n    gamma_max: float = 0.74\n    lam_override: float = 0.62\n    k_total: int = 50\n    kdensity: int = 18\n    delta: float\
    \ = 0.04\n    metric: str = 'cosine'\n    cap: float = 2.0\n    rng_seed: int = 0\n    ae_epochs: int = 5 # Small number of epochs for PoC\n    ae_batch_size: int = 256 # Batch size for AE training\n\n    # --- New Parameter for Candidate Pool Size ---\n    candidate_pool_size: int = 512 # TUNED: Increased candidate pool size as per Praxis V's suggestion\n\n\n    # --- Preprocessing: Generalization Test Preprocessing (from pre-normalized) ---\n    print(\"  Preprocessing: Generalization Test (Sourcing from adata.layers['normalized'] and re-normalizing without log1p)...\")\n    adata.X = adata.layers['normalized'].copy()\n    normalize_log1p_inplace_flexible(adata, 1e4, apply_log1p=False)\n\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv_mask = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n\n    batches_np = adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').cat.codes.values\n\n    Xh_np = adata.X[:, hv_mask]\n    Xd_np = (Xh_np.A if\
    \ sp.issparse(Xh_np) else Xh_np).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n    # Adaptive Xd Variance Scaling (for pre-normalized input)\n    target_mean_var = 0.8944\n    current_mean_var = np.mean(Xd_np.var(axis=0))\n    if current_mean_var > 1e-8:\n        scaling_factor = np.sqrt(target_mean_var / current_mean_var)\n        Xd_np = Xd_np * scaling_factor\n        print(f\"  Xd variance scaled. Original mean var: {current_mean_var:.4f}, Target mean var: {target_mean_var:.4f}, Scaling factor: {scaling_factor:.4f}\")\n        print(f\"  New Xd.var stats (after mean scaling): Mean={np.mean(Xd_np.var(axis=0)):.4f}, Std={np.std(Xd_np.var(axis=0)):.4f}, Min={np.min(Xd_np.var(axis=0)):.4f}, Max={np.max(Xd_np.var(axis=0)):.4f}\")\n    else:\n        print(f\"  Skipping Xd mean variance scaling: current_mean_var is {current_mean_var:.4f}.\")\n\n    # Convert Xd to JAX array for FW-PCA and AE input\n    Xd_jax = jnp.asarray(Xd_np, dtype=jnp.float32)\n\n    # Max variance clip for FW-PCA (applied within\
    \ _fw_weight_by_var for pre-normalized data)\n    max_var_g_clip_value = 10.2247\n\n\n    # --- Path 1: Generate Embedding (X_emb) --- (Still using PCA for embedding path for this PoC)\n    print(\"  Generating Embedding (X_emb) via SOTA Embedding Path (+ FW-PCA, Combat) [using PCA]...\")\n    Xw_emb_jax = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd_jax, alpha=alpha_emb, max_var_g_clip=max_var_g_clip_value)\n    ad_emb = ad.AnnData(np.asarray(Xw_emb_jax), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=rng_seed)\n    ad_pc_combat_input = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc_combat_input, key='batch')\n    X_emb_result = np.asarray(ad_pc_combat_input.X, dtype=np.float32)\n\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = X_emb_result\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric, random_state=rng_seed)\n\n    # --- Path 2: Generate Graph (connectivities, distances) with\
    \ Adaptive Local Correction ---\n    print(\"  Generating Graph (connectivities, distances) via SOTA Graph Path (+ FW-PCA, Adaptive Local Correction) [using Autoencoder]...\")\n    Xw_graph_jax = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd_jax, alpha=alpha_g, max_var_g_clip=max_var_g_clip_value) # Feature-weighted HVG data as JAX array\n\n    # Replace PCA with Autoencoder for Zg (Flax implementation)\n    original_dim = Xw_graph_jax.shape[1]\n    latent_dim = n_pcs_graph\n\n    ae_model = Autoencoder(original_dim, latent_dim)\n    rng_key = jax.random.PRNGKey(rng_seed)\n\n    # Train AE\n    print(f\"  Training Autoencoder for {ae_epochs} epochs with batch size {ae_batch_size}...\")\n    state = train_autoencoder(ae_model, Xw_graph_jax, original_dim, latent_dim, ae_epochs, ae_batch_size, rng_key)\n\n    # FIXED: Extract latent space properly using the trained autoencoder's encoder\n    # Create a separate encoder model and extract its parameters from the trained autoencoder\n    encoder_model = Encoder(latent_dim)\n\
    \    # Initialize encoder with proper parameter structure\n    encoder_init_params = encoder_model.init(rng_key, Xw_graph_jax[0:1])\n    # Copy the trained encoder parameters from the autoencoder state\n    encoder_params = {'params': state.params['encoder']}\n    # Apply the encoder to get latent representation\n    Zg_jax = encoder_model.apply(encoder_params, Xw_graph_jax)\n    Zg_np = np.asarray(Zg_jax, dtype=np.float32)\n\n    print(\"  Applying novel Adaptive Local Correction...\")\n    B_np = one_hot_batches(batches_np)\n    Zhat_np = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B_np, Zg_np, l2=l2)\n\n    nn_density = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=kdensity + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n    nn_density.fit(Zg_np)\n    d_k, _ = nn_density.kneighbors(Zg_np, return_distance=True)\n    d_k = d_k[:, -1]\n    d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k) + 1e-8)\n    normalized_dist = (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)\n    density_factor = 1.0 - normalized_dist\n\n    var_total = Zg_np.var(axis=0,\
    \ ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat_np.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    gamma_global = np.minimum(gamma_max, float(lam_override) * R2).astype(np.float32)\n\n    gamma_local = gamma_global[np.newaxis, :] * density_factor[:, np.newaxis]\n    Zcorr_np = Zg_np - (Zhat_np * gamma_local)\n\n    print(f\"  Correction strength stats: Global_Gamma_Mean={np.mean(gamma_global):.3f}, Local_Gamma_Mean={np.mean(gamma_local):.3f}\")\n\n    Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr_np.astype(np.float32), batches_np,\n                                         k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                         delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                                         rng_seed=rng_seed, candidate_pool_size=candidate_pool_size)\n\n    # --- Combine outputs into final AnnData ---\n    output = ad.AnnData(\n        obs=adata.obs[[]],\n        var=adata.var[[]],\n        uns={\n            'dataset_id': adata.uns.get('dataset_id',\
    \ 'unknown'),\n            'normalization_id': adata.uns.get('normalization_id', 'unknown'),\n            'method_id': 'aethel_gen_test_robust_kq512',\n            'embedding_params': {\n                'alpha_emb': alpha_emb, 'n_pcs_emb': n_pcs_emb, 'metric': metric\n            },\n            'graph_params': {\n                'alpha_g': alpha_g, 'n_pcs_graph': n_pcs_graph, 'l2': l2,\n                'gamma_max': gamma_max, 'lam_override': lam_override,\n                'k_total': k_total, 'kdensity': kdensity, 'delta': delta,\n                'metric': metric, 'cap': cap,\n                'ae_epochs': ae_epochs, 'ae_batch_size': ae_batch_size,\n                'candidate_pool_size': candidate_pool_size\n            }\n        },\n        obsm={\n            'X_emb': adata.obsm['X_emb']\n        },\n        obsp={\n            'connectivities': Cg,\n            'distances': Dg\n        }\n    )\n\n    output.uns['neighbors'] = {\n        'connectivities_key': 'connectivities',\n \
    \       'distances_key': 'distances',\n        'params': {\n            'n_neighbors': k_total,\n            'method': 'bbsg',\n            'metric': metric,\n            'n_pcs': n_pcs_graph,\n            'k_density': kdensity,\n            'delta': delta,\n            'candidate_pool_size': candidate_pool_size\n        }\n    }\n\n    print(f\"✓ Aethel's Gen Test Robustness (Candidate Pool Size 512) Complete. Embedding shape: {output.obsm['X_emb'].shape}, Graph connectivities shape: {output.obsp['connectivities'].shape}\")\n    return output\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n[Aethel's Gen Test Robustness] Candidate Pool Size 512 on Pre-Normalized Data\n  Preprocessing: Generalization Test (Sourcing from adata.layers['normalized']\
    \ and re-normalizing without log1p)...\n  Xd variance scaled. Original mean var: 452.0700, Target mean var: 0.8944, Scaling factor: 0.0445\n  New Xd.var stats (after mean scaling): Mean=0.8944, Std=2.0540, Min=0.0000, Max=48.7834\n  Generating Embedding (X_emb) via SOTA Embedding Path (+ FW-PCA, Combat) [using PCA]...\n  Generating Graph (connectivities, distances) via SOTA Graph Path (+ FW-PCA, Adaptive Local Correction) [using Autoencoder]...\n  Training Autoencoder for 5 epochs with batch size 256...\n  Applying novel Adaptive Local Correction...\n  Correction strength stats: Global_Gamma_Mean=0.071, Local_Gamma_Mean=0.063\n✓ Aethel's Gen Test Robustness (Candidate Pool Size 512) Complete. Embedding shape: (20000, 60), Graph connectivities shape: (20000, 20000)\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/8bb97705-6a04-4bf9-9040-b7935640a4cd/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 8bb97705-6a04-4bf9-9040-b7935640a4cd\n\n\
    \nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1614 | 1 | EtC Combat PCs + Ridge + Efficient Equal-Quota Graph + UMAP | Lumen I | 1120 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1613 | 1 | Ridge GraphFWPCA + neighbors meta — kq=1024, mutual=1.0, row-norm=True (δ=0.12, k=50, kd=22) |\
    \ Praxis V | 1120 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1612 | 1 | Ridge GraphFWPCA + neighbors meta — kq=256, mutual=1.0, row-norm=True (δ=0.12, k=50, kd=22) | Praxis V | 1120 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1611 | 1 | Aethel's Gen Test Robustness (3/N): Candidate Pool Size 512 on Pre-Normalized | Aethel I | 1119 | 0.7011 | 0.649 | 0.645 | 0.244 | 0.277 | 0.957 | 0.664 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.970 | 0.639 |\n| 1610 | 1 | Generalization Test: ComBat Embedding + Simple BBKNN Graph | Fathom I | 1118 | 0.6272 | 0.640 | 0.660 | 0.222 | 0.360 | 0.875 | 0.705 | 1.000 | 0.992 | 0.033 | 0.787 |\n| 1609 | 1 | Ridge GraphFWPCA (no mutual, no row-norm) — kq=1024 (k=50, kd=22, δ=0.12, seed=0) | Praxis V | 1118 | 0.5180 | 0.720 | 0.667 | 0.205 | 0.299 | 0.889 | 0.717 | 0.000 | 0.980 | 0.096 | 0.608 |\n| 1608 | 1 | Ridge GraphFWPCA (no mutual, no row-norm) — kq=256 (k=50, kd=22, δ=0.12, seed=0) | Praxis V | 1118 | 0.5196 | 0.720 | 0.667 | 0.205 | 0.317 | 0.889 | 0.717 | 0.000 | 0.980\
    \ | 0.096 | 0.606 |\n| 1607 | 1 | RINT Generalization Test (2/2): RINT + Simple EtC on Normalized Data | Nous I | 1118 | 0.4635 | 0.150 | 0.907 | 0.129 | 0.278 | 0.460 | 0.321 | 1.000 | 0.925 | 0.342 | 0.123 |\n| 1606 | 1 | RINT Generalization Test (1/2): Simple EtC on Normalized Data | Nous I | 1118 | 0.4988 | 0.167 | 0.859 | 0.141 | 0.306 | 0.583 | 0.399 | 1.000 | 0.871 | 0.405 | 0.257 |\n| 1605 | 1 | Baseline: ComBat on PCA | Fathom I | 1117 | 0.4546 | 0.415 | 0.516 | 0.208 | 0.348 | 0.890 | 0.649 | 0.000 | 0.991 | 0.003 | 0.528 |\n\nPage 1 of 162 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-162, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help\
